{{Gaza genocide sidebar |expanded=recognition and denial}}
Since its foundation in 1948, [[Israel]] has been accused of carrying out [[genocide]] against [[Palestinians]] during the [[Israeli–Palestinian conflict]]. A wide consensus of scholars have concluded that Israel's actions during the [[Gaza war]] since 2023 [[Gaza genocide|constitute genocide]], although debate continues over whether Israel's treatment of Palestinians since the [[Nakba]]—prior to 2023—also constitutes genocide, and whether such actions are continuous or limited to specific periods or events. This treatment has also been characterised as "slow-motion genocide",{{sfn|Lendman|2010|pp=30–33}}{{sfn|Nijim|2023|p=177}} as well as a corollary or expression of [[Zionism as settler colonialism|settler colonialism]] and [[indigenous land theft]].{{sfn|Rashed|Short|2012|pp=1143, 1148–1149}}{{sfn|Docker|2012|p=2}}<ref>{{harvnb|El-Affendi|2024|p=1}}; {{harvnb|Short|2016|p=10}}; {{harvnb|Shaw|2013|p=4}}; {{harvnb|Rashed|Short|Docker|2014|pp=13–15}}; {{harvnb|Usher|2006|pp=10–14, 28–29}}; {{harvnb|Saldívar|2010|pp=826–827, 828–829}}; {{harvnb|Khoury|2018|pp=117–118}}; {{harvnb|Nijim|2020|pp=41–47}}; {{harvnb|Samudzi|2024|pp=7–8}}; {{harvnb|United Nations|2022}}; {{harvnb|Adhikari|Carmichael|Jones|Kapila|2018|p=148}}; {{harvnb|Üngör|2024|pp=3–4|ps=: "or Israeli settler colonial genocide"}}</ref> Those who believe Israel's actions constitute genocide point to the entrenched [[anti-Palestinian racism]], [[anti-Arab racism]], [[Islamophobia]] and genocidal rhetoric in Israeli society, and point to events such as the [[Nakba]], the [[Sabra and Shatila massacre]], the [[blockade of the Gaza Strip]], the [[2014 Gaza War]], and the 2023–present Gaza war as particularly pertinent genocidal episodes.{{sfn|Center for Constitutional Rights|2016|p=6}}<ref>{{harvnb|Eghbariah|2023}}; {{harvnb|Shaw|2013|pp=1–7}}; {{harvnb|Nijim|2023|pp=173–174, 176–177}}</ref> International law and genocide scholars have accused Israeli officials of using [[dehumanising]] language.<ref>{{harvnb|Docker|2012|p=16}}; {{harvnb|Munayyer|2015}}; {{harvnb|Bruneau|Kteily|2017}}; {{harvnb|Kuttab|2023}}; {{harvnb|Wintour|2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=17 October 2023 |title=Public Statement: Scholars Warn of Potential Genocide in Gaza |url=https://twailr.com/public-statement-scholars-warn-of-potential-genocide-in-gaza/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231117143548/https://twailr.com/public-statement-scholars-warn-of-potential-genocide-in-gaza/ |archive-date=17 November 2023 |work=Third World Approaches to International Law Review |quote=Statements of Israeli officials since 7 October 2023 suggest that beyond the killings and restriction of basic conditions for life perpetrated against Palestinians in Gaza, there are also indications that the ongoing and imminent Israeli attacks on the Gaza Strip are being conducted with potentially genocidal intent. Language used by Israeli political and military figures appears to reproduce rhetoric and tropes associated with genocide and incitement to genocide. Dehumanising descriptions of Palestinians have been prevalent. Israeli Defense Minister Yoav Gallant declared on 9 October that "we are fighting human animals and we act accordingly". He subsequently announced that Israel was moving to "a full-scale response" and that he had "removed every restriction" on Israeli forces, as well as stating: "Gaza won't return to what it was before. We will eliminate everything." On 10 October, the head of the Israeli army's Coordinator of Government Activities in the Territories (COGAT), Maj. Gen. Ghassan Alian, addressed a message directly to Gaza residents: "Human animals must be treated as such. There will be no electricity and no water, there will only be destruction. You wanted hell, you will get hell". The same day, Israeli army spokesperson Daniel Hagari acknowledged the wanton and intentionally destructive nature of Israel's bombing campaign in Gaza: "The emphasis is on damage and not on accuracy."}}</ref>

On 29 December 2023, [[South Africa]] filed a [[South Africa's genocide case against Israel|case against Israel]] at the [[International Court of Justice]], alleging that Israel's conduct in Gaza during the 2023 war amounted to genocide.<ref name="SA-Genocide2">{{cite news |last1=Roelf |first1=Wendell |last2=Sterling |first2=Toby |date=29 December 2023 |title=South Africa files genocide case against Israel at World Court |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/south-africa-seeks-international-court-justice-genocide-order-against-israel-2023-12-29/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231231123102/https://www.reuters.com/world/south-africa-seeks-international-court-justice-genocide-order-against-israel-2023-12-29/ |archive-date=31 December 2023 |access-date=29 December 2023 |work=[[Reuters]]}}</ref><ref name="Associated Press2">{{cite news |title=South Africa launches case at top UN court accusing Israel of genocide in Gaza |url=https://apnews.com/article/south-africa-israel-un-court-palestinians-genocide-ffe672c4eb3e14a30128542eaa537b21 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231231012340/https://apnews.com/article/south-africa-israel-un-court-palestinians-genocide-ffe672c4eb3e14a30128542eaa537b21 |archive-date=31 December 2023 |access-date=29 December 2023 |work=[[AP News]] |publisher=[[Associated Press]]}}</ref> South Africa asked the ICJ to issue provisional measures, including ordering Israel to halt its military campaign in Gaza.<ref name="SA-Genocide2"/> The Israeli government agreed to defend itself at the ICJ proceedings, while also denouncing South Africa's actions as "disgraceful" and accusing it of abetting "the modern heirs of the [[Nazis]]".<ref name="The Jerusalem Post2">{{cite news |last1=Lazaroff |first1=Tovah |date=2 January 2024 |title=Israel to defend itself at Int'l Court of Justice's genocide hearing on Gaza |url=https://www.jpost.com/breaking-news/article-780436 |access-date=2 January 2024 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |archive-date=6 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240106124511/https://www.jpost.com/breaking-news/article-780436 |url-status=live}}</ref> South Africa's case has been supported by [[South Africa's genocide case against Israel#Other international responses|a number of countries]].<ref>~{{bulleted list|
|{{cite news |date=8 January 2024 |title=Bolivia to support South Africa's ICJ genocide case against Israel |url=https://www.jpost.com/breaking-news/article-781214 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240108114420/https://www.jpost.com/breaking-news/article-781214 |archive-date=8 January 2024 |access-date=8 January 2024 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en-US}}
|{{harvnb|Shamim|2024}}
|{{harvnb|Human Rights Watch|2024}}
|{{cite news |last1=Salem |first1=Mohammed |last2=Al-Mughrabi |first2=Nidal |last3=Anthony |first3=Deutsch |title=Israel to face Gaza genocide charges at World Court |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israel-face-gaza-genocide-charges-world-court-2024-01-11/ |access-date=11 January 2024 |work=[[Reuters]] |date=10 January 2024 |quote="Colombia and Brazil expressed their support of South Africa late Wednesday." |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240112150047/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israel-face-gaza-genocide-charges-world-court-2024-01-11/ |archive-date=12 January 2024}}
|{{harvnb|Cuban Ministry of Foreign Affairs|2024}}
|{{cite news |last=Khaliq |first=Riyaz ul |date=10 January 2024 |title='Morally, politically:' Indonesia backs South Africa against Israel at ICJ |url=https://www.aa.com.tr/en/asia-pacific/-morally-politically-indonesia-backs-south-africa-against-israel-at-icj/3105258 |work=[[Anadolu Agency]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240111182315/https://www.aa.com.tr/en/asia-pacific/-morally-politically-indonesia-backs-south-africa-against-israel-at-icj/3105258 |archive-date=11 January 2024}}
|{{cite news |date=11 January 2024 |title=Iran backs South Africa's Gaza genocide case against Israel at ICJ |url=https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/iran-backs-south-africas-gaza-genocide-case-against-israel-at-icj/3105929 |work=[[Anadolu Agency]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240111181858/https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/iran-backs-south-africas-gaza-genocide-case-against-israel-at-icj/3105929 |archive-date=11 January 2024}}
|{{cite news |title=Iraq backs South Africa's case against Israel at ICJ |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/11/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-pounds-gaza-ahead-of-icj-genocide-hearing?update=2612364 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |access-date=12 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240114181936/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/1/11/israels-war-on-gaza-live-israel-pounds-gaza-ahead-of-icj-genocide-hearing?update=2612364 |archive-date=14 January 2024}}
}}</ref> On 26 January 2024, the ICJ issued a preliminary ruling finding that the claims in South Africa's filing were "plausible" and issued an order to Israel requiring them to take all measures within their power to prevent acts of genocide and to allow basic humanitarian services into Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |date=26 January 2024 |title=Read the I.C.J. ruling |url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/01/26/world/middleeast/icj-gaza-provisional-ruling.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240126202428/https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/01/26/world/middleeast/icj-gaza-provisional-ruling.html |archive-date=26 January 2024 |access-date=26 January 2024 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> 

Israel and the United States have rejected the assertion that the former is engaging in genocide.<ref>{{cite news |last=Magid |first=Jacob |date=7 November 2023 |title=White House spokesman appears to reject claim Israel committing 'genocide' |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/white-house-spokesman-appears-to-reject-claim-israel-committing-genocide/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231122120801/http://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/white-house-spokesman-appears-to-reject-claim-israel-committing-genocide/ |archive-date=22 November 2023 |work=[[Times of Israel]]}}</ref><ref name="Sales, 20212">{{cite news |last=Sales |first=Ben |date=27 May 2021 |title=People are accusing Israel of genocide. These human rights lawyers beg to differ |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/people-are-accusing-israel-of-genocide-these-human-rights-lawyers-beg-to-differ/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230323194510/https://www.timesofisrael.com/people-are-accusing-israel-of-genocide-these-human-rights-lawyers-beg-to-differ/ |archive-date=23 March 2023 |access-date=27 November 2023 |newspaper=[[Times of Israel]]}}</ref> While some scholars describe Palestinians as victims of genocide, others argue that what took place was [[ethnic cleansing]],{{sfn|Pappé|2006|}}{{sfn|Shaw|2013|pp=1–2}}{{sfn|Rashed|Short|Docker|2014|pp=9–10}} [[politicide]], spaciocide, [[cultural genocide]] or similar.<ref>{{harvnb|Rashed|Short|Docker|2014|pp=12–15}}; {{harvnb|Lentin|2008|p=10}}; {{harvnb|Lentin|2010|pp=20–21}}: "While neither 'categorial murder' nor genocide, the Nakba has been described as 'ethnic cleansing' (Pappé, 2006) or 'spaciocide' (Hanafi, 2005), perpetrated by self categorising 'Jews', 'Zionists', or 'Israelis', against people they categorised as 'Arabs'."</ref><ref name="genocide-denial12">{{cite magazine |last=Corn |first=David |date=3 November 2023 |title=During a Trip to Israel, Mike Johnson Connected With Far-Right Extremists |url=https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/11/mike-johnson-israel-extremists/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240102200828/https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/11/mike-johnson-israel-extremists/ |archive-date=2 January 2024 |access-date=2 January 2024 |magazine=[[Mother Jones (magazine)|Mother Jones]] |quote=During the trip, Johnson observed, "You hear in the US about how the Palestinians or the Arab people are oppressed in these areas, and have these terrible lives. None of that is true. We didn't see any of it."}}</ref>{{efn|The designation of genocide can also be dependent on the specific event talked about, as an example while Ilan Pappé does not consider the Nakba an act of genocide,{{sfn|Lentin|2010|pp=20–21}} he considers Israel's actions against Gaza in the [[Second Intifada]] and the 2008–2009 Gaza War, acts of genocide.<ref name="Pappé2008">{{cite news |last=Pappé |first=Ilan |author-link=Ilan Pappé |date=28 January 2008 |title=Genocide in Gaza, Ethnic Cleansing in the West Bank |url=https://countercurrents.org/Papp%C3%A9280108.htm |work=[[The Indypendent]] |access-date=16 February 2024 |via=[[Countercurrents.org|Countercurrents]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240118234838/https://countercurrents.org/Papp%C3%A9280108.htm |archive-date=18 January 2024 |url-status=dead }}</ref>{{sfn|Lentin|2010|p=142}}}} Some critics of the accusation have argued that charges of Israel committing genocide are commonly made by [[anti-Zionists]] with the aim of demonising or [[Legitimacy of the State of Israel|delegitimising Israel]].<ref name="Hirsh2">{{cite journal |last=Hirsh |first=David |author-link=David Hirsh |date=2015 |title=Anti Zionism and Antisemitism: Cosmopolitan Reflections |url=https://isgap.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/ISGAP-Working-Papers-David-Hirsh.pdf |journal=The Yale Papers: Antisemitism in Comparative Perspective |pages=106–107 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216073139/https://isgap.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/ISGAP-Working-Papers-David-Hirsh.pdf |archive-date=16 December 2023 |access-date=7 December 2023}}</ref>

