=== 20th century ===
==== Nakba ====
{{Main|Nakba}}

[[File:Tantura expulsion (997008136022405171).jpg|thumb|1948 expulsion of the [[Tantura]] women and children to [[Furaydis]]|alt=Women carrying bags while walking with men and children]]
{{Nakba}}

The Nakba was the violent displacement and dispossession of the Palestinian people, along with the destruction of their society, [[Culture of Palestine|culture]], identity, political rights, and [[Palestinian nationalism|national aspirations]].<ref name="NakbaDef2">{{harvnb|Abu-Laban|Bakan|2022|pp=511–512}};

{{harvnb|Manna|2022|pp=7–9}};

{{harvnb|Khalidi|2020|pp=60, 76, 82, 88–89}};

{{harvnb|Shenhav|2019|pp=48–51}};

{{harvnb|Bashir|Goldberg|2018|loc=Introduction}};

{{harvnb|Al-Hardan|2016|pp=xi, 2}};

{{harvnb|Rashed|Short|Docker|2014|p=1}};

{{harvnb|Masalha|2012|pp=1, 10–13}};

{{harvnb|Lentin|2010|loc=ch. 2}};

{{harvnb|Abu-Lughod|Sa'di|2007|pp=3, 8–9}}</ref> The Nakba began during the [[1948 Palestine war]]; the term [[ongoing Nakba]] has been used to describe the continued persecution and displacement of Palestinians by Israel throughout the Palestinian territories.<ref name="Ongoing2">{{harvnb|Sayigh|2023|pp=285 and 288 n. 12–13}};

{{harvnb|Pappé|2021|pp=70–71 and 80}};

{{harvnb|Khalidi|2020|p=75}};

{{harvnb|Shenhav|2019|p=49}};

{{harvnb|Bashir|Goldberg|2018|pp=7 and 33 n.4}};

{{harvnb|Rashed|Short|Docker|2014|pp=1 and 12–18}};

{{harvnb|Masalha|2012|pp=5, 12–14, 75 and 254}};

{{harvnb|Lentin|2010|pp=23, 111}};

{{harvnb|Abu-Lughod|Sa'di|2007|pp=10 and 18–19}};

{{harvnb|Ali|2012|pp=78–79}};

{{harvnb|Samudzi|2024|p=5}}</ref> Palestinians continued to be [[1949–1956 Palestinian expulsions|expelled]] after the war, and more Palestinian towns and villages were destroyed, with new Israeli settlements established in their place.<ref>{{harvnb|Sayigh|2023|p=281}};

{{harvnb|Khalidi|2020|pp=75 and 83}};

