Both Israel and Palestine frequently accuse the other of planning to commit genocide.{{sfn|Short|2016|p=70}}{{sfn|Samudzi|2024|p=1}}

In late 2023, various global leaders and officials voiced their perspectives on the Israel-Gaza conflict, with many labeling Israel's actions in Gaza as "genocide." Iranian Foreign Minister Hossein Amir-Abdollahian,<ref>{{cite news |date=13 October 2023 |title=Iran Accuses Israel of 'Genocide' Against the Palestinians in Gaza |url=https://english.aawsat.com/arab-world/4602621-iran-accuses-israel-‘genocide’-against-palestinians-gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231031095402/https://english.aawsat.com/arab-world/4602621-iran-accuses-israel-%E2%80%98genocide%E2%80%99-against-palestinians-gaza |archive-date=31 October 2023 |publisher=Asharq Al-Awsat}}</ref> Pakistani Foreign Minister [[Jalil Abbas Jilani]],<ref>{{cite news |title=FM Jilani equates Israeli strikes, blockade of Gaza to genocide against Palestinians |url=https://www.dawn.com/news/1781220/fm-jilani-equates-israeli-strikes-blockade-of-gaza-to-genocide-against-palestinians |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231024004155/https://www.dawn.com/news/1781220/fm-jilani-equates-israeli-strikes-blockade-of-gaza-to-genocide-against-palestinians |archive-date=24 October 2023 |publisher=[[Dawn (newspaper)|Dawn]]}}</ref> the [[Taliban]],<ref>{{cite web |date=18 October 2023 |title=The Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Islamic Emirate of Afghanistan condemns in the strongest terms the bombardment of the Al-Mamadani Hospital in Gaza by the Zionist forces and deems this act barbaric and a crime against humanity. |url=https://mfa.gov.af/en/the-ministry-of-foreign-affairs-of-the-islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-condemns-in-the-strongest-terms-the-bombardment-of-the-al-mamadani-hospital-in-gaza-by-the-zionist-forces-and-deems-this-act-barba/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117192320/https://mfa.gov.af/en/the-ministry-of-foreign-affairs-of-the-islamic-emirate-of-afghanistan-condemns-in-the-strongest-terms-the-bombardment-of-the-al-mamadani-hospital-in-gaza-by-the-zionist-forces-and-deems-this-act-barba/ |archive-date=17 January 2024 |access-date=17 January 2024 |website=[[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Afghanistan)]] |language=en-US |quote=We stand in solidarity with the Palestinians, and with countries and organizations calling for the immediate end of the ongoing genocide and bringing its perpetrators to justice.}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Sharma |first=Vasu |date=14 November 2023 |title=Decoding Pakistan and Afghanistan's Public Responses to the Israel-Hamas War |url=https://www.stimson.org/2023/decoding-pakistan-and-afghanistans-public-responses-to-the-israel-hamas-war/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117192321/https://www.stimson.org/2023/decoding-pakistan-and-afghanistans-public-responses-to-the-israel-hamas-war/ |archive-date=17 January 2024 |access-date=17 January 2024 |website=[[Stimson Center]] |language=en-US |quote=The Taliban's response to the current conflict is entirely in support of the Palestinians and calls out Israeli aggression for violating their rights and the sanctity of Al-Aqsa and other mosques in Palestine. In a series of tweets, Afghanistan's Ministry of Foreign Affairs referred to Israel's bombardment as a "genocide."}}</ref> Palestinian President [[Mahmoud Abbas]],<ref>{{cite news |last1=Mohamed |first1=Edna |last2=Najjar |first2=Farah |last3=Stepansky |first3=Joseph |title=Abbas: Israel's war on Gaza is 'genocide' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2488711 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231116004227/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2023/11/15/israel-hamas-war-live-israel-says-it-plans-to-raid-al-shifa-ministry?update=2488711 |archive-date=16 November 2023 |access-date=16 November 2023 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]}}</ref> Venezuelan President [[Nicolás Maduro]],<ref>{{cite web |date=10 October 2023 |title=Israel committing 'genocide' against Palestinian people |url=https://en.mehrnews.com/news/206973/Israel-committing-genocide-against-Palestinian-people |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231016175619/https://en.mehrnews.com/news/206973/Israel-committing-genocide-against-Palestinian-people |archive-date=16 October 2023 |access-date=12 October 2023 |website=[[Mehr News Agency|Mehr News]]}}</ref> and the [[Kurdistan Communities Union]] were among those who condemned Israel's actions.<ref>{{cite web |date=18 October 2023 |title=KCK: Attacks on the Palestinian people must stop |url=https://anfenglish.com/kurdistan/kck-attacks-on-the-palestinian-people-must-stop-69877 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240206185701/https://anfenglish.com/kurdistan/kck-attacks-on-the-palestinian-people-must-stop-69877 |archive-date=6 February 2024 |access-date=6 February 2024 |website=[[Firat News Agency]] |language=en |quote=Last night, the Israeli state launched an airstrike on a hospital in Gaza and unfortunately hundreds of people lost their lives in this attack. This attack is an attack of massacre and genocide.}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=5 November 2023 |title=Kalkan: We defend the just cause of the Palestinian people until the end |url=https://anfenglish.com/features/kalkan-we-defend-the-just-cause-of-the-palestinian-people-until-the-end-70128 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240206185914/https://anfenglish.com/features/kalkan-we-defend-the-just-cause-of-the-palestinian-people-until-the-end-70128 |archive-date=6 February 2024 |access-date=6 February 2024 |website=[[Firat News Agency]] |language=en |quote=Some time ago, Armenians in Karabakh were facing genocide. People were suffering. Now the same situation is happening in Gaza.}}</ref> [[Palestinian-American]] U.S. Congresswoman [[Rashida Tlaib]] accused President Biden of supporting this "genocide,"<ref name="droib2">{{cite news |last=Demirjian |first=Karoun |date=30 October 2023 |title=Democratic Rifts Over Israel Burst to the Forefront in Congress |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/30/us/politics/democrats-israel-gaza.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231108195142/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/10/30/us/politics/democrats-israel-gaza.html |archive-date=8 November 2023 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> leading to a resolution for censure against her by the Republican caucus, sponsored by [[Marjorie Taylor Greene]].<ref name="droib2"/> On 4 November, Tlaib released a video in which she directly accused [[President Biden]] of supporting "the genocide of the Palestinian people".<ref>{{cite news |date=4 November 2023 |title=US Representative Tlaib accuses Biden of supporting genocide against Palestinians |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us-representative-tlaib-accuses-biden-supporting-genocide-against-palestinians-2023-11-04/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231126213309/http://www.reuters.com/world/us-representative-tlaib-accuses-biden-supporting-genocide-against-palestinians-2023-11-04/ |archive-date=26 November 2023 |publisher=[[Reuters]]}}</ref>{{sfn|Narea|Samuel|2023}} [[Craig Mokhiber]] from the [[UN High Commissioner for Human Rights]] resigned, criticizing the organization for its response to the [[Gaza war]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Houghtaling |first=Ellie Quinlan |date=31 October 2023 |title=He Went There: Top U.N. Official Resigns Citing "Genocide" in Gaza |url=https://newrepublic.com/post/176538/top-un-official-resigns-citing-genocide-gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231113085903/https://newrepublic.com/post/176538/top-un-official-resigns-citing-genocide-gaza |archive-date=13 November 2023 |publisher=[[The New Republic]] |quote=Once again, we are seeing a genocide unfolding before our eyes, and the Organization that we serve appears powerless to stop it.}}</ref>{{sfn|Narea|Samuel|2023}} A day after Colombia withdrew its ambassador from Israel, President [[Gustavo Petro]] posted on [[Twitter|X]] in Spanish: "It's called genocide, they do it to remove the Palestinian people from Gaza and take it over. The head of the state who carries out this genocide is a criminal against humanity. Their allies cannot talk about democracy."<ref>{{cite news |date=2 November 2023 |title='Genocide', Colombia says as Latin American states condemn Israel over Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/2/genocide-colombia-says-as-latin-american-states-condemn-israel-over-gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231120090306/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/2/genocide-colombia-says-as-latin-american-states-condemn-israel-over-gaza |archive-date=20 November 2023 |publisher=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Rueda |first1=Manuel |title=Israel suspends military exports to Colombia over its president's criticism of Gaza siege |url=https://apnews.com/article/colombia-israel-petro-suspend-defense-exports-a92effbb531ea4631d25a8c1d32ede28 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022012058/https://apnews.com/article/colombia-israel-petro-suspend-defense-exports-a92effbb531ea4631d25a8c1d32ede28 |archive-date=22 October 2023 |access-date=20 October 2023 |work=[[Associated Press]]}}</ref> Leaders from Turkey,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Gumrukcu |first1=Tuvan |last2=Karakas |first2=Burcu |date=20 October 2023 |title=Turkey's Erdogan calls on Israel to stop its attacks on Gaza 'amounting to genocide' |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/turkeys-erdogan-calls-israel-stop-attacks-gaza-amounting-genocide-2023-10-20/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231102065137/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/turkeys-erdogan-calls-israel-stop-attacks-gaza-amounting-genocide-2023-10-20/ |archive-date=2 November 2023 |access-date=25 October 2023 |publisher=[[Reuters]]}}</ref> Brazil,<ref>{{cite web |last1=Verdélio |first1=Andreia |date=25 October 2023 |title=President Lula says war in the Middle East is genocide |url=https://agenciabrasil.ebc.com.br/en/politica/noticia/2023-10/president-lula-says-war-middle-east-genocide |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231126232437/https://agenciabrasil.ebc.com.br/en/politica/noticia/2023-10/president-lula-says-war-middle-east-genocide |archive-date=26 November 2023 |access-date=26 October 2023 |website=Agência Brasil}}</ref> and Syria also condemned Israel's actions.<ref>{{cite web |date=26 October 2023 |title=Syria denounced Western support for Israel's massacre in Gaza |url=https://www.plenglish.com/news/2023/10/26/syria-denounced-western-support-for-israels-massacre-in-gaza/#:~:text=Damascus%2C%20Oct%2026%20(Prensa%20Latina,led%20by%20the%20United%20States. |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231030202033/https://www.plenglish.com/news/2023/10/26/syria-denounced-western-support-for-israels-massacre-in-gaza/ |archive-date=30 October 2023 |access-date=26 October 2023 |website=Prensa Latina}}</ref>

The international response continued with various nations expressing strong condemnation. The [[Honduras|Honduran]] ministry of foreign affairs stated "Honduras energetically condemns the genocide and serious violations of international humanitarian law that the civilian Palestinian population is suffering in the Gaza Strip".<ref>{{cite news |last=Sforza |first=Lauren |date=6 November 2023 |title=These 8 countries have pulled ambassadors from Israel amid Hamas war |url=https://thehill.com/homenews/4296621-these-8-countries-have-pulled-ambassadors-from-israel-amid-hamas-war/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231118142216/https://thehill.com/homenews/4296621-these-8-countries-have-pulled-ambassadors-from-israel-amid-hamas-war/ |archive-date=18 November 2023 |access-date=23 November 2023 |work=[[The Hill (newspaper)|The Hill]]}}</ref> South Africa recalled its diplomatic mission from Israel and criticized Israel's ambassador for disparaging those "opposing the atrocities and genocide of the Israeli government".<ref>{{cite news |last=Magome |first=Mogomotsi |date=6 November 2023 |title=South Africa recalls ambassador and diplomatic mission to Israel and accuses it of genocide in Gaza |url=https://www.timesunion.com/news/world/article/south-africa-recalls-ambassador-and-diplomatic-18471371.php |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231123181620/https://www.timesunion.com/news/world/article/south-africa-recalls-ambassador-and-diplomatic-18471371.php |archive-date=23 November 2023 |access-date=6 November 2023 |website=Times Union |agency=[[Associated Press]]}}</ref> South African President [[Cyril Ramaphosa]] accused Israel of war crimes and acts "tantamount to genocide" in Gaza.<ref name="Imray2111232">{{cite news |last1=Imray |first1=Gerald |date=21 November 2023 |title=South African leader accuses Israel of war crimes |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-hamas-palestine-putin-xi-brics-0c070286b154198a36f0cf7440f973b5 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231130015556/https://apnews.com/article/israel-hamas-palestine-putin-xi-brics-0c070286b154198a36f0cf7440f973b5 |archive-date=30 November 2023 |access-date=28 November 2023 |publisher=[[AP News]]}}</ref> Iraqi Prime Minister [[Mohammed Al Sudani]] and Iranian President [[Ebrahim Raisi]] labeled the conflict a "genocide."<ref>{{cite news |last=Mahmoud |first=Sinan |date=6 November 2023 |title=Iraq and Iran describe Israel's war in Gaza as 'genocide' against Palestinians |url=https://www.thenationalnews.com/mena/iraq/2023/11/06/iraqi-pm-visits-tehran-on-first-stop-of-regional-tour-to-discuss-israel-gaza-war/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231114011548/https://www.thenationalnews.com/mena/iraq/2023/11/06/iraqi-pm-visits-tehran-on-first-stop-of-regional-tour-to-discuss-israel-gaza-war/ |archive-date=14 November 2023 |publisher=[[The National (Abu Dhabi)|The National]] |quote="Anyone who wants to contain this conflict and to prevent its spillover in the region should exert pressure on the authorities of the occupation to stop this aggression and the devastating and systematic killing, " Mr Al Sudani said. [...] "The aid from the United States to the Zionist regime [Israel] is encouraging them to kill and commit cruel acts of neglect against the Palestinian people, " Mr Raisi said. [...] "These horrible crimes against humanity are a genocide, which is carried out by the Zionist regime [Israel] with the support of the United States and certain European countries."}}</ref> Meanwhile, journalist [[Ishaan Tharoor]] highlighted that: "In protests around the world, in the corridors of the United Nations and in the angry chambers of social media, one word is getting louder and louder: genocide." with governments, UN rapporteurs, and scholars echoing this sentiment.<ref name="WAPO-specter2">{{cite news |last=Ishaan |first=Tharoor |date=7 November 2023 |title=Israel's war in Gaza and the specter of 'genocide' |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/11/07/genocide-israel-gaza-palestine/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231126233812/http://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2023/11/07/genocide-israel-gaza-palestine/ |archive-date=26 November 2023 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]}}</ref> The same month [[Jeremy Corbyn]], former leader of the [[UK Labour Party]], called for an [[International Criminal Court]] investigation.<ref>{{cite news |last=Corbyn |first=Jeremy |author-link=Jeremy Corbyn |date=6 November 2023 |title=The ICC must investigate the crime of genocide in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2023/11/6/the-icc-must-investigate-the-crime-of-genocide-in-gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231124075158/https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2023/11/6/the-icc-must-investigate-the-crime-of-genocide-in-gaza |archive-date=24 November 2023 |access-date=23 November 2023 |publisher=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]}}</ref>

UN experts reported that "grave violations" committed by Israeli forces against the Palestinians of Gaza "point to a genocide in the making" and cited evidence including "increasing genocidal incitement, overt intent to 'destroy the Palestinian people under occupation', loud calls for a 'second Nakba' in Gaza and the rest of the occupied Palestinian territory, and the use of powerful weaponry with inherently indiscriminate impacts, resulting in a colossal death toll and destruction of life-sustaining infrastructure."<ref>{{cite web |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=16 November 2023 |title=Gaza: UN experts call on international community to prevent genocide against the Palestinian people |url=https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/11/gaza-un-experts-call-international-community-prevent-genocide-against |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231224050530/https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2023/11/gaza-un-experts-call-international-community-prevent-genocide-against |archive-date=24 December 2023 |access-date=22 December 2023 |website=[[OHCHR]] |quote=Grave violations committed by Israel against Palestinians in the aftermath of 7 October, particularly in Gaza, point to a genocide in the making, UN experts said today. They illustrated evidence of increasing genocidal incitement, overt intent to "destroy the Palestinian people under occupation", loud calls for a 'second Nakba' in Gaza and the rest of the occupied Palestinian territory, and the use of powerful weaponry with inherently indiscriminate impacts, resulting in a colossal death toll and destruction of life-sustaining infrastructure.}}</ref>

Contrasting these views, Israel's Ambassador to the [[Philippines]], [[Ilan Fluss]], denied allegations of genocide, asserting Israel's efforts to minimize civilian casualties and target Hamas members.{{sfn|Antonio|2023|ps=: "Israeli Ambassador to the Philippines Ilan Fluss rejected the notion that his country is committing genocide in Gaza City, where a two-week war has erupted [...] their measures were targeting Hamas members, and they were "taking all measures to avoid having civilians affected" by attacks. "We are informing civilians even before attacks: keep away from Hamas' infrastructure and Hamas' facilities," [...] Hamas attacked Israel on Oct. 7, and killed at least 1,400 people, mostly civilians."}} [[National Security Advisor (United States)|US national security advisor]] [[John Kirby (admiral)|John Kirby]] stated that applying the term "genocide" to Israeli actions was "inappropriate," while emphasizing Hamas' stated intent "What Hamas wants, make no mistake about it, is genocide," explaining "[[Calls for the destruction of Israel|They want to wipe Israel off the map]]".<ref name="Lazaroff2">{{cite news |last=Lazaroff |first=Tovah |date=21 November 2023 |title=Kirby: word genocide thrown around inappropriately against Israel |url=https://www.jpost.com/international/article-774296 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121052003/https://www.jpost.com/international/article-774296 |archive-date=21 November 2023 |access-date=21 November 2023 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="Magid2">{{cite news |last=Magid |first=Jacob |date=21 November 2023 |title='Genocide' accusations by anti-Israel activists 'pretty inappropriate' — White House |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/genocide-accusations-by-anti-israel-activists-pretty-inappropriate-white-house/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121115636/https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/genocide-accusations-by-anti-israel-activists-pretty-inappropriate-white-house/ |archive-date=21 November 2023 |work=[[Times of Israel]] |quote="Israel is not trying to wipe the Palestinian people off the map. Israel is not trying to wipe Gaza off the map. Israel is trying to defend itself against a genocidal terrorist threat. So if we're going to start using that word, Fine. Let's use it appropriately," Kirby says.}}</ref>

In February 2024, law professor and [[United Nations special rapporteur]] on the right to food, Michael Fakhri, accused the state of Israel of being "culpable" of genocide, as according to Fakhri, firstly "Israel has announced its intention to destroy the Palestinian people, in whole or in part, simply for being Palestinian", and secondly Israel was denying food to Palestinians by halting humanitarian aid and "intentionally" destroying "small-scale fishing vessels, greenhouses and orchards in Gaza{{nbsp}}[...] We have never seen a civilian population made to go so hungry so quickly and so completely, that is the consensus among starvation experts. Israel is not just targeting civilians, it is trying to damn the future of the Palestinian people by harming their children."{{sfn|Lakhani|2024}}

=== Cultural discourse ===
{{See also|Cultural discourse about the Gaza genocide}}
[[File:Gas the Arabs painted in Hebron.jpg|right|thumb|Graffiti in [[Hebron]], in the [[Israeli-occupied territories|Israeli-occupied]] West Bank, calling for [[Gas chamber|the gassing]] of Arabs, above a [[Tag (graffiti)|tag]] for the right-wing group the [[Jewish Defense League]]<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Harkinson |first=Josh |date=11 March 2015 |title=Why are US taxpayers subsidizing right-wing Israeli settlers? |url=https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2015/03/hebron-fund-israeli-settlers-tax-exempt-irs-avaaz/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240123185054/https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2015/03/hebron-fund-israeli-settlers-tax-exempt-irs-avaaz/ |archive-date=23 January 2024 |access-date=22 January 2024 |magazine=[[Mother Jones (magazine)|Mother Jones]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Matar |first=Haggai |date=10 May 2014 |title=How I got involved in a 14-year-old girl's murder case |url=https://www.972mag.com/how-i-got-involved-in-a-14-year-old-girls-murder-case/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240122195518/https://www.972mag.com/how-i-got-involved-in-a-14-year-old-girls-murder-case/ |archive-date=22 January 2024 |access-date=22 January 2024 |magazine=[[+972 Magazine]] |language=en-US}}</ref>]]
Statements of genocidal intent have long been a feature of the Israeli cultural landscape, not least in the chant or slogan of "[[Death to Arabs]]" – a regular invocation at far-right Israeli protests and marches, such at the annual march marking "[[Jerusalem Day]]".<ref>{{cite journal |last=Sorek |first=Tamir |date=6 February 2025 |title=Mainstreaming a Genocidal Imagination in Israeli Society: Settler-Colonialism, Settler Anxiety, and Biblical Cues |journal=[[Journal of Genocide Research]] |issue=Forum: Israel-Palestine: Atrocity Crimes and the Crisis of Holocaust and Genocide Studies |pages=1–24 |doi=10.1080/14623528.2025.2456321|doi-access=free }}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |last=Ziv |first=Oren |date=30 May 2022 |title=WATCH: Jewish supremacists chant 'Death to Arabs' during Flag March |url=https://www.972mag.com/jewish-supremacists-flag-march-jerusalem/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231125022350/https://www.972mag.com/jewish-supremacists-flag-march-jerusalem/ |archive-date=25 November 2023 |magazine=[[+972 Magazine]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Doyle |first=Chris |date=2 June 2022 |title=Israel–Palestine: Would western media walk on eggshells if Arabs were chanting 'death to Jews'? |url=https://www.middleeasteye.net/opinion/israel-palestine-arabs-chanting-death-jews-western-media-eggshells |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230321053619/https://www.middleeasteye.net/opinion/israel-palestine-arabs-chanting-death-jews-western-media-eggshells |archive-date=21 March 2023 |work=[[Middle East Eye]]}}</ref>

In 2023, several high-profile individuals and groups voiced strong opinions on the Israel-Gaza conflict, with some labelling Israel's actions as genocide. Writer [[Jazmine Hughes]] left ''[[The New York Times]]'' after signing an open letter condemning Israel's actions in Gaza calling them "an attempt to conduct genocide".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Selk |first1=Avi |last2=Chery |first2=Samantha |date=4 November 2023 |title=N.Y. Times writer quits over open letter accusing Israel of 'genocide' |url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/media/2023/11/04/nyt-jazmine-hughes-resigns/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231118013610/https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/media/2023/11/04/nyt-jazmine-hughes-resigns/ |archive-date=18 November 2023 |newspaper=[[The Washington Post]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=26 October 2023 |title=Statement of Solidarity |url=https://www.writersagainstthewarongaza.com/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231124061259/https://www.writersagainstthewarongaza.com/ |archive-date=24 November 2023 |website=Writers against the war on Gaza}}</ref> Musician [[Macklemore]] expressed his view that the conflict is a genocide at a rally in Washington.<ref>{{cite magazine |last1=Moench |first1=Mallory |last2=Gordon |first2=Anna |date=5 November 2023 |title=Key Moments From the Pro-Palestinian Marches Across the U.S. |url=https://time.com/6331688/protest-marches-us-gaza-war-ceasefire/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231120191131/https://time.com/6331688/protest-marches-us-gaza-war-ceasefire/ |archive-date=20 November 2023 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|TIME]]}}</ref> Feminist scholars [[Angela Davis]] and [[Zillah Eisenstein]], among nearly 150 other signatories, signed an open letter which reads "We will not be silent when the bells of genocide ring. Silence is complicity."<ref>{{cite web |last=Zhang |first=Sharon |date=30 October 2023 |title=Over 140 Prominent Feminist Scholars Demand Ceasefire, End to Occupation in Gaza |url=https://truthout.org/articles/over-140-prominent-feminist-scholars-demand-ceasefire-end-to-occupation-in-gaza/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231117172657/https://truthout.org/articles/over-140-prominent-feminist-scholars-demand-ceasefire-end-to-occupation-in-gaza/ |archive-date=17 November 2023 |website=[[Truthout]]}}</ref> Mexican actress [[Melissa Barrera]] was reportedly fired from "[[Scream VII]]" for social media posts supporting Palestine and labelling Israel's actions as "genocide and ethnic cleansing".<ref>{{cite news |date=22 November 2023 |title=Susan Sarandon, Melissa Barrera dropped from Hollywood companies after comments on Israel–Hamas war |url=https://apnews.com/article/melissa-barrera-susan-sarandon-israel-palestine-scream-101895c5aafe2ec2f77e3dcda706e6ec |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231122183348/https://apnews.com/article/melissa-barrera-susan-sarandon-israel-palestine-scream-101895c5aafe2ec2f77e3dcda706e6ec |archive-date=22 November 2023 |work=[[Associated Press News]]}}</ref>

Russian-American author [[Masha Gessen]] when asked if what was happening in Gaza was a genocide said, "I think there are some fine distinctions between genocide and ethnic cleansing and I think that there are valid arguments for using both terms".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Gessen |first1=Masha |author1-link=Masha Gessen |date=21 December 2023 |title=Masha Gessen Responds to Controversy After Comparing Gaza to a Nazi Ghetto |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YU6kP9UqhGI&t=977s |website=[[YouTube]] |publisher=[[Amanpour and Company]] |language=en |format=video |access-date=15 January 2024 |archive-date=10 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240110030226/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YU6kP9UqhGI&t=977s |url-status=live}}</ref> When pressed further they stated, "it is at the very least ethnic cleansing". This was followed soon after [[Masha Gessen#Award controversy|controversy]] surrounding Gessen's reception of the [[Hannah Arendt Prize]] over remarks in a [[The New Yorker|New Yorker]] article critical of Israeli actions in the strip in which Gessen compared them to an Eastern European ghetto "being liquidated" by the Nazis.<ref name="GessenNY2">{{cite magazine |last1=Gessen |first1=Masha |author-link=Masha Gessen |date=9 December 2023 |title=In the Shadow of the Holocaust |url=https://www.newyorker.com/news/the-weekend-essay/in-the-shadow-of-the-holocaust |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240117043556/https://www.newyorker.com/news/the-weekend-essay/in-the-shadow-of-the-holocaust |archive-date=17 January 2024 |access-date=15 January 2024 |magazine=[[The New Yorker]]}}</ref> In December 2023, [[Olly Alexander]], set to represent the [[United Kingdom in the Eurovision Song Contest 2024|United Kingdom]] in the [[Eurovision Song Contest 2024]],<ref>{{cite news |last=Penna |first=Dominic |date=20 December 2023 |title=BBC urged to sack Eurovision entrant who called Israel an 'apartheid state' |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2023/12/20/bbc-pressure-olly-alexander-eurovision-israel-apartheid/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231223180327/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2023/12/20/bbc-pressure-olly-alexander-eurovision-israel-apartheid/ |archive-date=23 December 2023 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph|The Telegraph]] |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref> signed a letter by the LGBT association [[Voices4London]] accusing Israel of genocide against Palestinians.<ref>{{cite news |date=21 December 2023 |title=UK Eurovision act Olly Alexander criticised for signing statement calling Israel an 'apartheid state' and accusing it of genocide |url=https://news.sky.com/story/uk-eurovision-act-olly-alexander-criticised-for-signing-statement-calling-israel-an-apartheid-state-and-accusing-it-of-genocide-13035601 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240103135440/https://news.sky.com/story/uk-eurovision-act-olly-alexander-criticised-for-signing-statement-calling-israel-an-apartheid-state-and-accusing-it-of-genocide-13035601 |archive-date=3 January 2024 |work=[[Sky News]]}}</ref> This stance led to condemnation from the Israeli government and the [[Campaign Against Antisemitism]] (CAA), who asked the BBC to disallow Alexander's Eurovision participation. However, the BBC declined Israel's request, choosing not to sever ties with Alexander over his political views.<ref>{{cite news |last=Penna |first=Dominic |date=22 December 2023 |title=BBC will not stop Eurovision contestant expressing his political views |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2023/12/22/bbc-eurovision-contestant-olly-alexander-political-views/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231230131731/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2023/12/22/bbc-eurovision-contestant-olly-alexander-political-views/ |archive-date=30 December 2023 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |language=en-GB |issn=0307-1235}}</ref>

== Rhetoric ==
=== From Israeli officials ===
{{see also|Far-right politics in Israel#Statements from far-right ministers|Intent and incitement in the Gaza genocide}}

Those who have accused Israel of genocide have cited various statements made by Israeli government and military officials as evidence of intent to commit genocide. During the [[Gaza War (2008–2009)|2008–09 Gaza War]], Israeli Defense Minister [[Matan Vilnai]] said: "The more Qassam [rocket] fire intensifies and the rockets reach a longer range, they will bring upon themselves a bigger [[Names of the Holocaust#Shoah|Shoah]] because we will use all our might to defend ourselves." Colleagues said that his statement had meant "disaster" rather than "genocide".{{sfn|Rashed|Short|2012|p=1155}}{{sfn|Shaw|2010|pp=2–3}}<ref>{{cite news |last=McCarthy |first=Rory |date=1 March 2008 |title=Israeli minister warns of Holocaust for Gaza if violence continues |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2008/mar/01/israelandthepalestinians1 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240106192536/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2008/mar/01/israelandthepalestinians1 |archive-date=6 January 2024 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref>

Scholars, such as Mark Levene,{{sfn|Levene|2024|p=5}} Raz Segal, Luigi Daniele,{{sfn|Segal|Daniele|2024|p=1}} and Shmuel Lederman,{{sfn|Lederman|2024|pp=1–2}} alongside news outlets such as [[AP News]],<ref name="Goldenberg2">{{cite news |last=Goldenberg |first=Tia |date=18 January 2024 |title=Harsh Israeli rhetoric against Palestinians becomes central to South Africa's genocide case |url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-south-africa-genocide-hate-speech-97a9e4a84a3a6bebeddfb80f8a030724 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240305035421/https://apnews.com/article/israel-palestinians-south-africa-genocide-hate-speech-97a9e4a84a3a6bebeddfb80f8a030724 |archive-date=5 March 2024 |work=[[AP News]]}}</ref> have highlighted the increasing genocidal rhetoric in Israeli discourse since [[Benjamin Netanyahu]]'s 2015 prime ministership.{{sfn|Segal|Daniele|2024|pp=1–2}} They specifically highlight comments from [[Bezalel Smotrich]], [[Itamar Ben-Gvir]], and [[Ayelet Shaked]].<ref name="Goldenberg2"/>{{sfn|Segal|Daniele|2024|pp=1–2}}{{sfn|Lederman|2024|pp=1–2}} Levene applied [[A. Dirk Moses]]' analysis that "absolute securitization lends itself to collective targeting of human groups, more precisely civilians, regardless of issues of ethnos or genos."{{sfn|Levene|2024|p=2}} Statements made by Israeli politicians during the 2023–24 Gaza War were cited by [[South Africa]] in [[South Africa's genocide case against Israel|its allegation at the International Court of Justice]] that Israel has committed genocide against the Palestinian people.{{sfn|El-Affendi|2024|p=6}} 

On 28 October 2023, Netanyahu said Israelis were "committed to completely eliminating this evil from the world" and added: "You must remember what [[Amalek]] has done to you, says our Holy Bible. And we do remember." The quotation refers to [[Deuteronomy]] 25:17 in the [[Hebrew Bible]].{{efn|"Remember what Amalek did unto thee by the way as ye came forth out of Egypt; how he met thee by the way, and smote the hindmost of thee, all that were enfeebled in thy rear, when thou wast faint and weary; and he feared not God. Therefore it shall be, when the Lord thy God hath given thee rest from all thine enemies round about, in the land which the Lord thy God giveth thee for an inheritance to possess it, that thou shalt blot out the remembrance of Amalek from under heaven; thou shalt not forget." (''Deuteronomy 25:17–19'', [[Jewish Publication Society of America Version]])<ref name="isrgovtrsp2">{{cite speech |title=Statement by PM Netanyahu |last=Netanyahu |first=Benjamin |author-link=Benjamin Netanyahu |date=28 October 2023 |url=https://www.gov.il/en/departments/news/statement-by-pm-netanyahu-28-oct-2023 |access-date=9 February 2024 |location=Jerusalem |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231103014944/https://www.gov.il/en/departments/news/statement-by-pm-netanyahu-28-oct-2023 |archive-date=3 November 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref>{{sfn|El-Affendi|2024|p=2}} The phrase "Remember what Amalek did to you"({{langx|he|זכור את אשר עשה לך עמלק}}) is used in Holocaust memorials, including [[Yad Vashem]] and the Hague Jewish Monument.<ref name="yrosenberg2">{{cite magazine |last=Rosenberg |first=Yair |author-link=Yair Rosenberg |date=21 January 2024 |title=What Did Top Israel War Officials Really Say About Gaza? |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2024/01/israel-south-africa-genocide-case-fake-quotes/677198/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240205221304/https://www.theatlantic.com/international/archive/2024/01/israel-south-africa-genocide-case-fake-quotes/677198/ |archive-date=5 February 2024 |magazine=[[The Atlantic]]}}</ref>}} Critics say Netanyahu's reference to Amalek alludes to an incident in [[1 Samuel]] 15:3, in which God commands the Israelites to commit genocide against the Amalekites.{{efn|"Now go and smite Amalek, and utterly destroy all that they have, and spare them not; but slay both man and woman, infant and suckling, ox and sheep, camel and ass." (''1 Samuel 15:3, [[King James Version]]''){{sfn|Narea|Samuel|2023}}<ref name="McGreal 20232"/><ref name="Lanard 2023"/>}} Noah Lanard of ''[[Mother Jones (magazine)|Mother Jones]]'' described the Amalek verses as among the most violent in the Bible and said they have a long history of being used by Israelis on the far-right, such as [[Baruch Goldstein]], to justify killing Palestinians.<ref name="Lanard 2023">{{cite web |last=Lanard |first=Noah |date=3 November 2023 |title=The dangerous history behind Netanyahu's Amalek rhetoric |url=https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/11/benjamin-netanyahu-amalek-israel-palestine-gaza-saul-samuel-old-testament/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231124213319/https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2023/11/benjamin-netanyahu-amalek-israel-palestine-gaza-saul-samuel-old-testament/ |archive-date=24 November 2023 |access-date=6 November 2023 |website=[[Mother Jones (magazine)|Mother Jones]]}}</ref> [[Yair Rosenberg]] says the Deuteronomy verse refers to the need to remember an attack against the Jewish people.<ref name="yrosenberg2"/> [[National Public Radio|NPR]] issued a correction to indicate that Netanyahu had added a citation to Deuteronomy, rather than Samuel, in his speech, but added: "Both stories call for the Israelites to completely eliminate their attackers. In the Book of Deuteronomy, the text reads '[[Damnatio memoriae|blot out the memory]] of Amalek from under heaven'."<ref name="nprcorr2">{{cite news |date=7 November 2023 |title=Netanyahu's references to violent biblical passages raise alarm among critics |url=https://www.npr.org/2023/11/07/1211133201/netanyahus-references-to-violent-biblical-passages-raise-alarm-among-critics |work=Morning Edition |publisher=[[National Public Radio]] |archive-date=10 February 2024 |access-date=9 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240210045554/https://www.npr.org/2023/11/07/1211133201/netanyahus-references-to-violent-biblical-passages-raise-alarm-among-critics |url-status=live}}</ref> 

On 9 October 2023, Israeli Defense Minister [[Yoav Gallant]] said Israel would launch a "complete siege" of Gaza, with plans to cut off electricity, food, water and fuel supplies, saying: "We are fighting human animals and will act accordingly."{{sfn|Karantth|2023}} Gallant's statements were criticized as expressing genocidal intent towards Palestinians, and of calling for collective punishment of Gazan civilians.<ref>{{harvnb|Karantth|2023}}: "While it appears that Gallant was specifically referring to Hamas fighters in that comment, the rest of the minister's remarks called for further oppression of all people in Gaza by denying them basic human needs."; {{harvnb|Semerdjian|2024|p=1}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Schifrin |first1=Nick |last2=Sagalyn |first2=Dan |last3=Kopelev |first3=Sonia |last4=Warsi |first4=Zeba |date=11 January 2024 |title=Experts give 2 perspectives on accusations Israel is committing genocide in Gaza |url=https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/experts-give-2-perspectives-on-accusations-israel-is-committing-genocide-in-gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240223120304/https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/experts-give-2-perspectives-on-accusations-israel-is-committing-genocide-in-gaza |archive-date=23 February 2024 |work=[[PBS NewsHour]] |quote="They used Yoav Gallant, the defense minister's statement that he's going after — that they're fighting human animals. He says, oh, I just meant Hamas, but, in fact, if you listen to him, he was talking about the siege, which is of everybody in Gaza."}}</ref><ref name="Igwrd2">{{cite news |last=Baroud |first=Ramzy |date=23 October 2023 |title=Israel's Gaza war rooted in dehumanizing, genocidal language |url=https://www.arabnews.com/node/2396301 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231123234708/https://www.arabnews.com/node/2396301 |archive-date=23 November 2023 |access-date=24 November 2023 |work=Arab News}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=24 January 2024 |title=Corrections: Jan. 24, 2024 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/23/pageoneplus/corrections-jan-24-2024.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240129072451/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/23/pageoneplus/corrections-jan-24-2024.html |archive-date=29 January 2024 |work=[[The New York Times]] |quote="Gaza won't return to what it was before. There will be no Hamas. We will eliminate everything."}}</ref>  Israeli Minister of Finance Bezalel Smotrich stated that Israel had "returned [[Khan Yunis]] to the stone age".<ref>{{cite news |date=9 April 2024 |title=Smotrich: Sinwar senses weakness, only military pressure will return hostages |url=https://www.israelnationalnews.com/news/388213 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240410184325/https://www.israelnationalnews.com/news/388213 |archive-date=10 April 2024 |access-date=9 April 2024 |work=Israel National News |language=en}}</ref>

Other Israeli figures whose statements on the 2023 war have been cited by accusers include [[Ariel Kallner]], a [[Knesset member]] for [[Likud]], who said Israel's sole goal was "A [[Nakba]] that will overshadow the Nakba of 1948",<ref name="Igwrd2"/> and IDF spokesman [[Daniel Hagari]], who said Israeli forces would turn Gaza into a "city of tents" with the focus on "damage and not on accuracy".{{sfn|Narea|Samuel|2023}} [[Amichay Eliyahu]], a cabinet minister, and [[Tally Gotliv]], a Likud parliament member, have called for Israel to use nuclear weapons on Gaza. Gotliv said: "It's time for a doomsday weapon. Not flattening a neighborhood. Crushing and flattening Gaza." [[Galit Distel-Atbaryan]] said that Israelis should focus on "Erasing all of Gaza from the face of the earth" and either forcing the Gazans into Egypt or killing them.{{sfn|Narea|Samuel|2023}} [[Raz Segal]] said statements such as these represented a "textbook case of genocide": "If this is not special intent to destroy, I don't know what is."{{sfn|Narea|Samuel|2023}} [[Anshel Pfeffer]] says that Benjamin Netanyahu has tolerated extreme rhetoric, including "apocalyptic threats and conspiracy theories", from his allies to serve his own personal political interests.<ref>{{cite news |last=Pfeffer |first=Anshel |author-link=Anshel Pfeffer |date=20 November 2023 |title=Why Netanyahu Won't Shut Down the Crazy Talk About 'Resettling' Gaza |url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2023-11-20/ty-article/.premium/why-netanyahu-wont-shut-down-the-crazy-talk-about-resettling-gaza/0000018b-ee0b-d6a0-a7ff-ee7fa0c30000 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231213134016/http://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/2023-11-20/ty-article/.premium/why-netanyahu-wont-shut-down-the-crazy-talk-about-resettling-gaza/0000018b-ee0b-d6a0-a7ff-ee7fa0c30000 |archive-date=13 December 2023 |access-date=7 January 2024 |work=[[Haaretz]] |language=en}}</ref> 

Ramzy Baroud of ''[[Arab News]]'' compared the rhetoric from Israeli officials with the language used in Rwanda ahead of the [[Rwandan genocide]], such as the refrain by the [[Radio Television Libre des Mille Collines]] (RTLM) in Rwanda that [[Tutsi]]s were "cockroaches" and a 1983 quote from former Israeli army chief of staff [[Rafael Eitan]] that Arabs are like "drugged cockroaches in a bottle".<ref name="Igwrd2"/> Journalist [[Chris McGreal]], who won an [[Amnesty International Media Award]] for his reporting of the Rwandan genocide,<ref>{{cite news |date=26 November 2002 |title=Awards for Guardian journalists |url=https://www.theguardian.com/media/2002/nov/26/theguardian.pressandpublishing |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160312111654/http://www.theguardian.com/media/2002/nov/26/theguardian.pressandpublishing |archive-date=12 March 2016 |access-date=14 December 2016 |work=[[The Guardian]] |location=London}}</ref> also described the rhetoric against Palestinians as being "eerily familiar" to the rhetoric used against Tutsis.<ref>{{cite news |last=McGreal |first=Chris |author-link=Chris McGreal |date=16 October 2023 |title=The language being used to describe Palestinians is genocidal |url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/oct/16/the-language-being-used-to-describe-palestinians-is-genocidal |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121075045/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/oct/16/the-language-being-used-to-describe-palestinians-is-genocidal |archive-date=21 November 2023 |work=[[The Guardian]] |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

On 14 November 2023, Israel's finance minister Bezalel Smotrich said he welcomed "the initiative of the voluntary emigration of Gaza Arabs to countries around the world". He said that "the State of Israel will no longer be able to accept the existence of an independent entity in Gaza".<ref>{{cite news |date=14 November 2023 |title=Israeli minister calls for voluntary emigration of Gazans |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-minister-calls-voluntary-emigration-gazans-2023-11-14/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121235512/https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-minister-calls-voluntary-emigration-gazans-2023-11-14/ |archive-date=21 November 2023 |access-date=15 November 2023 |work=[[Reuters]] |language=en}}</ref> Critics, such as [[Palestinian National Initiative]] president [[Mustafa Barghouti]], have likened the statement to a call for ethnic cleansing.<ref name="Israeli minister2">{{cite news |date=14 November 2023 |title=Israeli minister supports 'voluntary migration' of Palestinians in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/14/israeli-minister-supports-voluntary-migration-of-palestinians-in-gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121065831/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/14/israeli-minister-supports-voluntary-migration-of-palestinians-in-gaza |archive-date=21 November 2023 |access-date=15 November 2023 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |language=en}}</ref> The Palestinian Authority's Ministry of Foreign affairs accused Israel of engaging in a "genocide" supported by Smotrich.<ref name="Israeli minister2"/> Likud Intelligence Minister [[Gila Gamliel]] said the international community should promote the "voluntary resettlement" of Palestinians in Gaza to sites around the globe.<ref>{{cite news |date=19 November 2023 |title=Likud minister suggests world should promote 'voluntary resettlement' of Gazans |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/likud-minister-suggests-world-should-promote-voluntary-resettlement-of-gazans/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231121193914/https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/likud-minister-suggests-world-should-promote-voluntary-resettlement-of-gazans/ |archive-date=21 November 2023 |work=[[The Times of Israel]]}}</ref> A [[Channel 12 (Israel)|Channel 12]] survey reported that 44 percent of responders said they were in favor of a renewal of Jewish settlement in Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |date=18 November 2023 |title=Survey shows substantial support for renewal of Jewish settlement in Gaza after war |url=https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/survey-shows-substantial-support-for-renewal-of-jewish-settlement-in-gaza-after-war |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231122180446/https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/survey-shows-substantial-support-for-renewal-of-jewish-settlement-in-gaza-after-war |archive-date=22 November 2023 |work=[[The Times of Israel]]}}</ref>

[[File:Free Palestine will not be cancelled (53309781090).jpg|thumb|Protester in [[Berlin]] on 4 November 2023, holding a "Stop the Genocide in Gaza" sign]]
In November 2023, Israel's former justice minister, Ayelet Shaked, spoke of transforming Khan Younis into a soccer field with "the assistance of God and the IDF". He said Israel should pressure countries worldwide into accepting quotas of Gazan refugees, ranging from 20,000 to 50,000 per country.<ref>{{cite news |date=22 November 2023 |title=Ayelet Shaked makes provocative statements on relocating population in Gaza |url=https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231122-ayelet-shaked-makes-provocative-statements-on-relocating-population-in-gaza/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231223103717/https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231122-ayelet-shaked-makes-provocative-statements-on-relocating-population-in-gaza/ |archive-date=23 December 2023 |work=[[Middle East Monitor]]}}</ref> [[Otzma Yehudit]] MK [[Limor Son Har-Melech]], said: "there is no escape from returning and fully controlling the Gaza Strip", including "extensive and flourishing settlement" across "the entire length and width of the strip".<ref>{{cite news |date=24 November 2023 |title=Otzma Yehudit MK calls for control of Gaza Strip |url=https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/politics-and-diplomacy/article-774881 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240119104402/https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/politics-and-diplomacy/article-774881 |archive-date=19 January 2024 |access-date=15 January 2024 |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |language=en-US}}</ref> David Azoulay, the local council head of the town of [[Metula]], said the people of Gaza should be transported to "Lebanon's shores where there are enough refugee camps". He said: "the entire Gaza Strip should be emptied and levelled flat, just like in [[Auschwitz concentration camp|Auschwitz]]. Let it become a museum, showcasing the capabilities of the State of Israel and dissuading anyone from living in the Gaza Strip" and "demonstrating the madness of the people who lived there". His statements were condemned by the [[Auschwitz-Birkenau State Museum]].<ref>{{cite news |date=18 December 2023 |title=Israel council leader says Gaza 'should become Auschwitz' |url=https://www.newarab.com/news/israel-council-leader-says-gaza-should-become-auschwitz |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231222074527/https://www.newarab.com/news/israel-council-leader-says-gaza-should-become-auschwitz |archive-date=22 December 2023 |access-date=22 December 2023 |work=[[The New Arab]] |language=en}}</ref>

=== From American officials since 2023 ===
{{Main|Intent and incitement in the Gaza genocide#Statements by American officials}}

In the Florida legislature, [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] Representative [[Angie Nixon]], supporting a ceasefire resolution early in the Gaza war, highlighted the high death toll of Palestinians questioning how many had to die before a ceasefire was called for,{{efn|Around 10,000 Palestinians had been reported dead at the time of the debate.{{sfn|Salam|2023|ps=: "We are at 10,000 dead Palestinians. How many will be enough?"}}}} [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] Representative [[Michelle Salzman]] replied instantly "All of them". Salzman's remark, perceived as a call for genocide, led to calls for censure or resignation from Nixon and the Florida chapter of the [[Council on American–Islamic Relations|Council on American-Islamic Relations]] called for her to be censured or to resign.<ref>{{cite news |last=Mitrovica |first=Andrew |title=Getting away with a call to genocide in Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2023/11/20/all-of-them |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216224755/https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2023/11/20/all-of-them |archive-date=16 December 2023 |access-date=3 December 2023 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last=Salam |first=Erum |date=10 November 2023 |title=Outrage grows after 'chilling call for genocide' by Florida Republican |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/10/florida-republican-michelle-salzman-palestine |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231204212337/https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/10/florida-republican-michelle-salzman-palestine |archive-date=4 December 2023 |access-date=3 December 2023 |work=[[The Guardian]] |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref> [[Council on American–Islamic Relations|CAIR]]-Florida Executive Director Imam Abdullah Jaber said in a statement: "This chilling call for genocide by an American lawmaker is the direct result of decades of dehumanization of the Palestinian people by advocates of Israeli apartheid and their eager enablers in government and the media."<ref>{{cite news |date=10 November 2023 |title=CAIR-Florida Condemns Lawmaker's Call for Killing of 'All' Palestinians, Calls for GOP Censure and Public Repudiation |url=https://www.cair.com/press_releases/cair-florida-condemns-lawmakers-call-for-killing-of-all-palestinians-calls-for-gop-censure-and-public-repudiation/ |work=[[Council on American-Islamic Relations]] |archive-date=10 February 2024 |access-date=3 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240210140515/https://www.cair.com/press_releases/cair-florida-condemns-lawmakers-call-for-killing-of-all-palestinians-calls-for-gop-censure-and-public-repudiation/ |url-status=live}}</ref>{{primary inline|date=February 2026}}

In October 2023, Republican Florida governor [[Ron DeSantis]] said "If you look at how [people in Gaza] behave, not all of them are Hamas, but they are all anti-Semitic" and called for a "swift and lethal response."<ref>{{cite news |last=Alafriz |first=Olivia |date=14 October 2023 |title=DeSantis: U.S. should not accept Gaza refugees |url=https://www.politico.com/news/2023/10/14/desantis-they-are-all-anti-semitic-00121587 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240102085245/https://www.politico.com/news/2023/10/14/desantis-they-are-all-anti-semitic-00121587 |archive-date=2 January 2024 |access-date=2 January 2024 |work=[[Politico]] |language=en}}</ref> Republican US Congressman [[Max Miller (politician)|Max Miller]], on [[Fox News]], stated that Palestine is "about to get eviscerated{{nbsp}}... to turn that into a parking lot." He said there should be "no rules of engagement" during Israel's bombardment of Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |date=26 October 2023 |title=US congressman: 'Palestine will be turned into a parking lot' |url=https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231026-us-congressman-palestine-will-be-turned-into-a-parking-lot/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231028030424/https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20231026-us-congressman-palestine-will-be-turned-into-a-parking-lot/ |archive-date=28 October 2023 |work=[[Middle East Monitor]]}}</ref> Miller also questioned the accuracy of the [[Gaza Health Ministry]]'s claim that 10,000 people have been killed in Gaza, saying that he believes many of those killed have been "Hamas terrorists", not innocent civilians.<ref>{{cite web |last=Eaton |first=Sabrina |date=17 November 2023 |title=U.S. Rep. Max Miller defends Israel's conduct of Hamas war after visit to Tel Aviv |url=https://www.cleveland.com/news/2023/11/us-rep-max-miller-defends-israels-conduct-of-hamas-war-after-visit-to-tel-aviv.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216072034/https://www.cleveland.com/news/2023/11/us-rep-max-miller-defends-israels-conduct-of-hamas-war-after-visit-to-tel-aviv.html |archive-date=16 December 2023 |access-date=3 December 2023 |website=cleveland.com |language=en}}</ref> Republican U.S. Representative [[Brian Mast]] compared all Palestinians to Nazis in November on the House floor, stating "I don’t think we would so lightly throw around the term 'innocent Nazi civilians' during World War II. It is not a far stretch to say there are very few innocent Palestinian civilians."<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Otten |first=Tori |date=1 November 2023 |title=Republican Representative Directly Compares All Palestinians to Nazis |url=https://newrepublic.com/post/176559/republican-representative-brian-mast-compares-palestinians-nazis |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240203033548/https://newrepublic.com/post/176559/republican-representative-brian-mast-compares-palestinians-nazis |archive-date=3 February 2024 |access-date=3 February 2024 |magazine=[[The New Republic]] |issn=0028-6583}}</ref> On 31 January 2024, Mast said that Palestinian babies are not innocent civilians but "terrorists" who should be killed, that more infrastructure in Gaza needs to be destroyed, and "It would be better if you kill all the terrorists and kill everyone who are supporters."<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Otten |first=Tori |date=1 February 2024 |title=GOP Congressman Says Dead Palestinian Babies Aren't All That Innocent |url=https://newrepublic.com/post/178679/gop-congressman-brian-mast-dead-palestinian-babies-not-innocent |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201235221/https://newrepublic.com/post/178679/gop-congressman-brian-mast-dead-palestinian-babies-not-innocent |archive-date=1 February 2024 |access-date=3 February 2024 |magazine=[[The New Republic]] |issn=0028-6583}}</ref>

Republican [[Tennessee|Tennesse]] representative [[Andy Ogles]] said "I think we should kill them all." [[Arkansas]] senator [[Tom Cotton]] remarked "As far as I’m concerned, Israel can bounce the rubble in Gaza." [[Michigan]] representative [[Tim Walberg]] said "We shouldn’t be spending a dime on humanitarian aid. It [Gaza] should be like Nagasaki and Hiroshima. Get it over quick." [[South Carolina]] senator [[Lindsey Graham]] called the genocide a "[[religious war]]" and said he sides with Israel, calling on it to do "whatever the hell you have to do to defend yourself; level the place."<ref name=":0">{{Cite news |last=Harb |first=Ali |date=7 October 2025 |title='Not a punchline': 15 dehumanising quotes on Gaza atrocities by US figures |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/10/7/not-a-punchline-15-dehumanising-quotes-on-gaza-atrocities-by-us-figures |access-date=12 October 2025 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251010130016/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/10/7/not-a-punchline-15-dehumanising-quotes-on-gaza-atrocities-by-us-figures |archive-date=10 October 2025}}</ref> Florida representative [[Randy Fine]] called for Gaza to be nuked like [[Atomic bombings of Hiroshima and Nagasaki|Nagasaki and Hiroshima]] and made numerous statements endorsing genocide and starvation in Gaza, such as "There is no suffering adequate for these animals. May the streets of Gaza overflow with blood," "Release the hostages. Until then, starve away," "There is no starvation. Everything about the 'Palestinian' cause is a lie," and "Kill. Them. All. #NoMercy #BombsAway."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Carroll |first=Rosaleen |date=29 July 2025 |title=AIPAC denies pulling Randy Fine endorsement after derogatory comments on Gaza starvation - AL-Monitor: The Middle East's leading independent news source since 2012 |url=https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2025/07/aipac-denies-pulling-randy-fine-endorsement-after-derogatory-comments-gaza |access-date=12 October 2025 |website=[[Al-Monitor]] |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250807025818/https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2025/07/aipac-denies-pulling-randy-fine-endorsement-after-derogatory-comments-gaza |archive-date=7 August 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=29 July 2025 |title=Randy Fine 'dropped by AIPAC' over Gaza starvation remarks |url=https://www.newarab.com/news/randy-fine-dropped-aipac-over-gaza-starvation-remarks |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250809092532/https://www.newarab.com/news/randy-fine-dropped-aipac-over-gaza-starvation-remarks |archive-date=9 August 2025 |access-date=12 October 2025 |work=[[The New Arab]] |language=en-EN |url-status=live }}</ref> Former presidential candidate in the [[2024 Republican Party presidential primaries]], [[Nikki Haley]], wrote "finish them" on an Israeli bomb bound for Gaza.<ref>{{Cite news |date=29 May 2024 |title=Nikki Haley writes 'Finish Them!' on Israeli bomb bound for Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2024/5/29/nikki-haley-writes-finish-them-on-israeli-bomb-bound-for-gaza |access-date=12 October 2025 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |language=en |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250919122412/https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2024/5/29/nikki-haley-writes-finish-them-on-israeli-bomb-bound-for-gaza |archive-date=19 September 2025}}</ref>

Former Republican Representative [[Michele Bachmann]] appearing in December on [[Charlie Kirk|''The Charlie Kirk Show'']] claimed all Palestinians were "clever assassins" and that they should be forcefully relocated to Iran. She received a round of applause from the audience, while Kirk replied that US policies should be more like those of the current Israeli government.<ref>{{cite web |date=18 December 2023 |title=Michele Bachmann Calls for Ethnic Cleansing in Gaza: 'They Need To Be Removed From That Land' |url=https://www.mediaite.com/tv/michele-bachmann-calls-for-ethnic-cleansing-in-gaza-they-need-to-be-removed-from-that-land/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231224135124/https://www.mediaite.com/tv/michele-bachmann-calls-for-ethnic-cleansing-in-gaza-they-need-to-be-removed-from-that-land/ |first=Michael |last=Luciano|archive-date=24 December 2023 |access-date=19 December 2023 |website=[[Mediaite]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=Media Matters Staff |date=18 December 2023 |title=Michelle Bachmann to Charlie Kirk: "It's time that Gaza ends. The 2 million people who live there, they are clever assassins. They need to be removed from that land." |url=https://www.mediamatters.org/charlie-kirk/michelle-bachmann-charlie-kirk-its-time-gaza-ends-2-million-people-who-live-there-they |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231219113014/https://www.mediamatters.org/charlie-kirk/michelle-bachmann-charlie-kirk-its-time-gaza-ends-2-million-people-who-live-there-they |archive-date=19 December 2023 |access-date=19 December 2023 |website=[[Media Matters for America]] |language=en}}</ref>

Ahmad Abuznaid, the executive director of the US Campaign for Palestinian Rights (USPCR) said that "There is a bipartisan effort to dehumanise the Palestinian people," referring especially to President Joe Biden voicing doubt over the accuracy of the Palestinian death count and attacks on Palestinian American Congresswoman Rashida Tlaib for her [[criticism of Israel]]'s military offensive.<ref>{{cite news |last=Harb |first=Ali |title=Anti-Palestinian sentiment rises amid bipartisan US support for Israel |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/14/anti-palestinian-sentiment-rises-amid-bipartisan-us-support-for-israel |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217071455/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/11/14/anti-palestinian-sentiment-rises-amid-bipartisan-us-support-for-israel |archive-date=17 December 2023 |access-date=3 December 2023 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |language=en}}</ref>

== Responses to the accusation ==
[[File:Bristol Palestine Solidarity March 4th November 2023 (53311833359).jpg|thumb|A protester holds a poster stating "Not in our name, Jews against genocide," at a pro-Palestine march in [[Bristol]], United Kingdom, 4 November 2023]]
The accusation of genocide has been largely rejected by [[Israelis]].{{sfn|Pappé|2010|pp=201–205}}<ref name="Plight2">{{cite book |last1=Polya |first1=Gideon |title=The Plight of the Palestinians: A Long History of Destruction |date=2010 |publisher=[[Palgrave Macmillan]] |isbn=978-0-230-10792-2 |pages=39–42 |language=en |chapter=Ongoing Palestinian Genocide |doi=10.1057/9780230107922_3 |chapter-url=https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1057/9780230107922_3 |archive-date=24 June 2021 |access-date=12 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210624201251/https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1057/9780230107922_3 |url-status=live}}</ref> Despite most Israelis rejecting the accusation of genocide, some Israelis and many in the [[Jewish diaspora]] – including several [[Holocaust survivors]] – have protested against the Israeli government, claiming that such accusations are true.<ref>{{harvnb|Pappé|2010|pp=201–205}}; {{harvnb|Segal|2023}}; {{harvnb|JTA|Kampeas|2021}}; {{harvnb|Center for Constitutional Rights|2016|pp=6–7}}</ref><ref name="JVP2">{{cite web |date=11 October 2023 |title=Jewish Voice for Peace calls on all people of conscience to stop imminent genocide |url=https://www.jewishvoiceforpeace.org/2023/10/11/statement23-10-11/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231116181005/https://www.jewishvoiceforpeace.org/2023/10/11/statement23-10-11/ |archive-date=16 November 2023 |work=[[Jewish Voice for Peace]] |quote=The Israeli government has declared a genocidal war on the people of Gaza. As an organization that works for a future where Palestinians and Israelis and all people live in equality and freedom, we call on all people of conscience to stop imminent genocide of Palestinians.}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Rocca |first1=Ryan |last2=Carty |first2=Matt |date=10 November 2023 |title=Protest held at Toronto's Union Station over Israel-Hamas conflict |url=https://globalnews.ca/news/10081243/toronto-union-station-pro-palestine-protest/ |access-date=9 April 2024 |work=[[Global News]] |language=en-CA |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240409223813/https://globalnews.ca/news/10081243/toronto-union-station-pro-palestine-protest/ |archive-date=9 April 2024}}</ref> 

Historian [[Simon Sebag Montefiore]] says that "Jews are now accused of the very crimes they themselves have suffered [...] when no genocide has taken place or been intended", with the effect that the word has "been so devalued by its metaphorical abuse that it has become meaningless".<ref name="SSMAtlantic2">{{cite magazine |last1=Montefiore |first1=Simon Sebag |author-link=Simon Sebag Montefiore |date=27 October 2023 |title=The Decolonization Narrative Is Dangerous and False |url=https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2023/10/decolonization-narrative-dangerous-and-false/675799/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20231028061758/https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2023/10/decolonization-narrative-dangerous-and-false/675799/ |archive-date=28 October 2023 |access-date=29 October 2023 |magazine=[[The Atlantic]]}}</ref> In 2015, sociologist [[David Hirsh]] said there has never been a genocide of Palestinians, and that there was no evidence of genocide in Gaza. Hirsh says that accusations of genocide against Israel – whether in Gaza, the West Bank, or Lebanon – are commonly made by anti-Zionists to demonize Israel and "oversimplify the complex dynamics of the Israeli-Palestinian conflict".<ref name="Hirsh2"/> Zionist history professor [[Robert S. Wistrich]] says the genocide accusation is "purely fictional".<ref>{{cite journal |last=Wistrich |first=Robert S. |date=2014 |title=Gaza, Hamas, and the Return of Antisemitism |url=https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/23739770.2014.11446601 |journal=[[Israel Journal of Foreign Affairs]] |volume=8 |issue=3 |pages=35–48 |doi=10.1080/23739770.2014.11446601 |s2cid=142072208 |access-date=7 December 2023 |archive-date=7 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231207180752/https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/23739770.2014.11446601 |url-status=live |url-access=subscription}}</ref>

U.S. Secretary of State [[Antony Blinken]] has called the genocide accusation against Israel "meritless".<ref>{{cite news |last=Samuels |first=Ben |date=9 January 2024 |title=Blinken: Genocide Charge Against Israel Is 'Meritless'; Palestinians Must Be Allowed Return to North Gaza |url=https://www.haaretz.com/us-news/2024-01-09/ty-article/.premium/blinken-genocide-charge-against-israel-meritless-palestinians-must-be-allowed-return/0000018c-ef8f-da6b-abdd-ffcf48d60000 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240109203811/https://www.haaretz.com/us-news/2024-01-09/ty-article/.premium/blinken-genocide-charge-against-israel-meritless-palestinians-must-be-allowed-return/0000018c-ef8f-da6b-abdd-ffcf48d60000 |archive-date=9 January 2024 |access-date=10 January 2024 |work=[[Haaretz]]}}</ref> U.S. [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic Party]] Representative [[Ritchie Torres]] calls the characterisation "[[blood libel]]".<ref>{{cite news |last=Fandos |first=Nicholas |date=11 November 2023 |title=Two Young Democratic Stars Collide Over Israel and Their Party's Future |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/11/nyregion/aoc-torres-israel-gaza.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231118155151/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/11/nyregion/aoc-torres-israel-gaza.html |archive-date=18 November 2023 |access-date=11 November 2023 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref> Conservative American radio talk show host [[Dennis Prager]] says that characterising the conflict as a genocide against the Palestinians is [[antisemitic]].<ref name="Prager&Telushkin_20032">{{cite book |last1=Prager |first1=Dennis |author1-link=Dennis Prager |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=wAeeCwAAQBAJ&pg=PR19 |title=Why the Jews?: The Reason for Antisemitism |last2=Telushkin |first2=Joseph |publisher=[[Simon & Schuster]] |year=2003 |isbn=978-0-7432-4620-0 |page=xix |language=English}}</ref>

In May 2024, [[NYU Langone Health]] fired Hesen Jabr, a Muslim Palestinian-American nurse, after she called Israel's actions in Gaza "genocide" during an award acceptance speech.<ref>{{cite news |last=Oladipo |first=Gloria |date=31 May 2024 |title=New York hospital fires nurse after calling Gaza war a 'genocide' in speech |url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/31/new-york-university-hospital-fires-nurse-gaza-war-genocide |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240602163328/https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/31/new-york-university-hospital-fires-nurse-gaza-war-genocide |archive-date=2 June 2024 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref>

== Victims ==
=== Deaths ===
[[File:Timeline_of_Israel-Palestine_fatalities_2008-2023.png|alt=A bar chart from 2008 to before October 2023. 6,407 Palestinians have been killed during this time frame, while a smaller 308 Israelis have been killed.|thumb|[[Israeli casualties of war|Israeli]] and [[Palestinian casualties of war|Palestinian deaths]] preceding the Gaza war in 2023. Most were civilians.<ref name="Deaths2">{{cite web |title=Data on casualties |url=https://www.ochaopt.org/data/casualties |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231120083937/https://www.ochaopt.org/data/casualties |archive-date=20 November 2023 |access-date=14 October 2023 |website=[[United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs]]}}</ref><ref name="alfonseca2">{{cite news |last1=Alfonseca |first1=Kiara |date=11 October 2023 |title=Palestinian civilians suffer in Israel-Gaza crossfire as death toll rises |url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/palestinian-civilians-suffer-israel-hamas-crossfire-death-toll/story?id=103828889 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231012150320/https://abcnews.go.com/International/palestinian-civilians-suffer-israel-hamas-crossfire-death-toll/story?id=103828889 |archive-date=12 October 2023 |access-date=12 October 2023 |work=[[ABC News (United States)|ABC News]]}}</ref>]]
[[Ilan Pappé]] reported in 2008 that since the year 2000 "almost 4,000 Palestinians have been killed by Israeli forces, half of them children, and more than 20,000 wounded."{{efn|Most of these occurred during the Second Intifada where, from 29 September 2000 to 1 January 2005, 3,179<ref name=statspage>{{cite web |url=http://212.150.54.123/casualties_project/stats_page.cfm |title=Breakdown of Fatalities: 27 September 2000 through 1 January 2005 |publisher=[[International Institute for Counter-Terrorism]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070703195937/http://212.150.54.123/casualties_project/stats_page.cfm |archive-date=3 July 2007}} Full report: {{cite web |first=Don |last=Radlauer |date=29 September 2002 |url=http://212.150.54.123/articles/articledet.cfm?articleid=439 |title=An Engineered Tragedy: Statistical Analysis of Casualties in the Palestinian – Israeli Conflict, September 2000 – September 2002 |publisher=[[International Institute for Counter-Terrorism]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070928191559/http://212.150.54.123/articles/articledet.cfm?articleid=439 |archive-date=28 September 2007}}</ref><ref name="BBCstats">{{cite news |title=Intifada toll 2000–2005 |url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/middle_east/3694350.stm |access-date=10 November 2012 |work=[[BBC News]] |date=8 February 2005 |archive-date=17 January 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150117121043/http://news.bbc.co.uk/1/hi/world/middle_east/3694350.stm |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="un2009jan9">{{cite web |url=http://www.ochaopt.org/documents/ocha_opt_gaza_humanitarian_situation_report_2009_01_09_english.pdf |title=Field Update on Gaza from the Humanitarian Coordinator |date=9 January 2009 |publisher=[[United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs]] |access-date=28 September 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150924055012/http://www.ochaopt.org/documents/ocha_opt_gaza_humanitarian_situation_report_2009_01_09_english.pdf |archive-date=24 September 2015}}</ref>–3,354<ref name="casualties2">{{cite web |url=http://www.btselem.org/english/statistics/casualties.asp?sD=29&sM=09&sY=2000&eD=26&eM=12&eY=2008&filterby=event&oferet_stat=before |title=B'Tselem – Statistics – Fatalities |publisher=[[B'Tselem]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100701064428/http://www.btselem.org/english/statistics/Casualties.asp?sD=29&sM=09&sY=2000&eD=26&eM=12&eY=2008&filterby=event&oferet_stat=before |archive-date=1 July 2010}}</ref> Palestinians were killed.}} According to data from the [[United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs]], 6,735 Palestinians had been killed from 1 January 2008, to 6 October 2023.<ref name="Deaths2"/>{{efn|1,116<ref>{{cite news |last=Lappin |first=Yaakov |date=2009 |url=https://www.jpost.com/israel/idf-releases-cast-lead-casualty-numbers |title=IDF releases Cast Lead casualty numbers |work=[[The Jerusalem Post]] |access-date=5 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201228033510/https://www.jpost.com/israel/idf-releases-cast-lead-casualty-numbers |archive-date=28 December 2020}}</ref>–1,417<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.pchrgaza.org/files/PressR/English/2008/36-2009.html |title=Confirmed figures reveal the true extent of the destruction inflicted upon the Gaza Strip; Israel's offensive resulted in 1,417 dead, including 926 civilians, 255 police officers, and 236 fighters. |date=2009 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090612193512/http://www.pchrgaza.org/files/PressR/English/2008/36-2009.html |access-date=5 January 2024 |archive-date=12 June 2009}}</ref> Palestinian deaths in the [[Gaza War (2008–2009)]].<br/>
2,125–2,310 Palestinian deaths in the [[2014 Gaza War]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.ohchr.org/Documents/HRBodies/HRCouncil/CoIGaza/A_HRC_CRP_4.doc |title=Report of the detailed findings of the independent commission of inquiry established pursuant to Human Rights Council resolution S-21/1 |date=23 June 2015 |website=[[OHCHR]] |access-date=15 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231228154326/https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/Documents/HRBodies/HRCouncil/CoIGaza/A_HRC_CRP_4.doc |archive-date=28 December 2023}}</ref>{{sfn|Nijim|2023|pp=179–180}}<br/>
250+ Palestinian deaths in the [[2021 Israel–Palestine crisis]].<ref>{{cite web |title=2021 was the deadliest year since 2014, Israel killed 319 Palestinians in oPt 5-year record in house demolitions: 895 Palestinians lost their homes |url=https://www.btselem.org/press_releases/20220104_in_deadliest_year_since_2014_israel_killed_319_palestinians_in_opt |publisher=[[B'Tselem]] |access-date=4 January 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220104225644/https://www.btselem.org/press_releases/20220104_in_deadliest_year_since_2014_israel_killed_319_palestinians_in_opt |archive-date=4 January 2022}}</ref>}}

====During the Gaza war====
{{Main|Casualties of the Gaza war}}

During the ongoing Gaza war, which began on 7 October 2023, a Reliefweb report released 18 November 2023, which labels Israel's actions in Gaza as a genocide, reported that 15,271 Palestinians in Gaza had been killed, 32,310 Palestinians had been injured, and an estimated 41,500 were unaccounted for.<ref>{{cite web |author=Euro-Med Monitor |author-link=Euro-Mediterranean Human Rights Monitor |date=18 November 2023 |title=Friday 17 November: Twenty thousand Palestinians believed to be killed in Israel's genocide of Gaza |url=https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/friday-17-november-twenty-thousand-palestinians-believed-be-killed-israels-genocide-gaza-enar |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231226003110/https://reliefweb.int/report/occupied-palestinian-territory/friday-17-november-twenty-thousand-palestinians-believed-be-killed-israels-genocide-gaza-enar |archive-date=26 December 2023 |access-date=25 December 2023 |website=Reliefweb}}</ref> Multiple news and academic outlets have subsequently reported on updated figures, with at least 20,000 Palestinians having been killed in [[Gaza Strip|Gaza]], an estimated 70% of whom were women and children.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Faddoul |first1=Alix |last2=Shannon |first2=Geordan |last3=Asghar |first3=Khudejha |last4=Boukari |first4=Yamina |last5=Smith |first5=James |last6=Neilson |first6=Amy |date=18 December 2023 |title=The health dimensions of violence in Palestine: a call to prevent genocide |url=https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(23)02751-4/fulltext |journal=[[The Lancet]] |volume=403 |issue=10421 |pages=25–26 |doi=10.1016/S0140-6736(23)02751-4 |pmid=38128558 |s2cid=266357297 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231221154829/https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(23)02751-4/fulltext |archive-date=21 December 2023 |url-access=subscription}}</ref><ref>{{harvnb|Thomas|2023}}; {{harvnb|AP News|2023a}}; {{harvnb|Sawafta|Fick|2023}}; {{harvnb|Euro-Med Human Rights Monitor|2023}}; {{harvnb|Burga|2023}}</ref> Per the [[Gaza Health Ministry]] and Government Information Office by 3 January 2024, over 22,300 people had been confirmed dead.<ref name="cas1tmp42">{{cite news |date=3 January 2024 |title=Health Ministry In Hamas-run Gaza Says War Death Toll Hits 22,313 |url=https://www.barrons.com/news/health-ministry-in-hamas-run-gaza-says-war-death-toll-hits-22-313-584e999b?refsec=topics_afp-news |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240103101715/https://www.barrons.com/news/health-ministry-in-hamas-run-gaza-says-war-death-toll-hits-22-313-584e999b?refsec=topics_afp-news |archive-date=3 January 2024 |access-date=3 January 2024 |publisher=[[Barron's]]}}</ref> About 7,000 people are missing, likely buried under the rubble.<ref>{{cite news |title=Deaths in Gaza surpass 14,000, according to its authorities |url=https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2023/11/23/deaths-in-gaza-surpass-14000-according-to-its-authorities |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231201143821/https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2023/11/23/deaths-in-gaza-surpass-14000-according-to-its-authorities |archive-date=1 December 2023 |access-date=28 November 2023 |newspaper=[[The Economist]] |issn=0013-0613}}</ref> Over 52,000 have been wounded.{{sfn|Thomas|2023}}{{sfn|AP News|2023a}} 

Indirect Palestinian deaths from disease in Gaza are expected to be much higher due to the intensity of the conflict, destruction of health care infrastructure, lack of food, water, shelter, and safe places for civilians to flee, and reduction in [[UNRWA]] funding; 186,000 Palestinians or more may have died as a result of the conflict according to a July 2024 conservative estimate by [[Rasha Khatib]], [[Martin McKee]], and [[Salim Yusuf]] published in [[The Lancet]].<ref name="KhatibMcKeeYusuf">{{cite journal |last1=Khatib |first1=Rasha |last2=McKee |first2=Martin |author2-link=Martin McKee |last3=Yusuf |first3=Salim |author3-link=Salim Yusuf |title=Counting the dead in Gaza: difficult but essential |journal=[[The Lancet]] |publisher=Elsevier BV |year=2024 |volume=404 |issue=10449 |pages=237–238 |issn=0140-6736 |doi=10.1016/s0140-6736(24)01169-3 |pmid=38976995 |url=https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(24)01169-3/fulltext |quote=Armed conflicts have indirect health implications beyond the direct harm from violence. Even if the conflict ends immediately, there will continue to be many indirect deaths in the coming months and years from causes such as reproductive, communicable, and non-communicable diseases. The total death toll is expected to be large given the intensity of this conflict; destroyed health-care infrastructure; severe shortages of food, water, and shelter; the population's inability to flee to safe places; and the loss of funding to UNRWA, one of the very few humanitarian organisations still active in the Gaza Strip. In recent conflicts, such indirect deaths range from three to 15 times the number of direct deaths. Applying a conservative estimate of four indirect deaths per one direct death to the 37,396 deaths reported, it is not implausible to estimate that up to 186,000 or even more deaths could be attributable to the current conflict in Gaza. Using the 2022 Gaza Strip population estimate of 2,375,259, this would translate to 7·9% of the total population in the Gaza Strip. |archive-date=27 September 2024 |access-date=28 July 2024 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20240927011250/https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(24)01169-3/fulltext |url-status=live |url-access=subscription}}</ref> [[Michael Spagat]] criticized their methodology, saying that the projection "lacks a solid foundation and is implausible".<ref name="Bigg NYT">{{Cite news |last=Bigg |first=Matthew Mpoke |date=11 July 2024 |title=Fighting Isn't the Only Killer of Gazans Amid the War, Researchers Say |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/11/world/middleeast/gaza-war-death-toll-lancet.html |access-date=11 July 2024 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240712123712/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/11/world/middleeast/gaza-war-death-toll-lancet.html%20 |archive-date=12 July 2024}}</ref> Even so, Spagat allowed it was "fair to call attention to the fact that not all of the deaths are going to be direct violent ones" and has called the death toll in Gaza "staggeringly high".<ref name="Horton et al.">{{Cite news |first1=Jake |last1=Horton |first2=Shayan |last2=Sardarizadeh |first3=Adam |last3=Durbin |date=16 May 2024 |title=Gaza war: Why is the UN citing lower death toll for women and children? |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-69014893 |access-date=12 July 2024 |work=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240711140750/https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-69014893 |archive-date=11 July 2024}}</ref><ref name="Bigg NYT"/>

=== Displacement ===
[[1948 Palestinian expulsion and flight|In 1948]], more than 700,000 Palestinians<ref name="750k2"/> – about half of prewar [[Mandatory Palestine]]'s Arab population – fled from their homes or were expelled by [[Zionist]] militias and, later, the Israeli army<ref>{{harvnb|Ibish|2018}}; {{harvnb|Hazkani|2019}}; {{harvnb|Warf|Charles|2020}}; {{harvnb|Gerber|2008}}; {{harvnb|Petersen-Overton|Schmidt|Hersh|2010|p=49}}; {{harvnb|Natour|2015|p=81}}</ref><ref>{{harvnb|Slater|2020|p=406}}: "There is no serious dispute among Israeli, Palestinian, or other historians about the central facts of the Nakba. All of the leading Israeli New Historians—particularly Morris, Shlaim, Pappé, and Flapan—extensively examined the issue and revealed the facts. Other accounts have reached the same conclusions. For example, see Ben-Ami, "A War to Start All Wars"; Rashid Khalidi, "The Palestinians and 1948"; Walid Khalidi, "Why Did the Palestinians Leave, Revisited"; Masalha, ''Expulsion of the Palestinians''; Raz, Bride and the Dowry. Reviewing the evidence marshaled by Morris and others, Tom Segev concluded that "most of the Arabs in the country, approximately 400,000, were chased out and expelled during the first stage of the war. In other words, before the Arab armies invaded the country" (''Haaretz'', July 18, 2010). Other estimates have varied concerning the number of Palestinians who fled or were expelled before the May 1948 Arab state attack; Morris estimated the number to be 250,000–300,000 (''The Birth of the Palestinian Refugee Problem Revisited'', 262); Tessler puts it at 300,000 (''A History of the Israeli-Palestinian Conflict'', 279); Pappé's estimate is 380,000 (''The Making of the Arab-Israeli Conflict'', 96). In another recent review of the evidence, the Israeli historian Daniel Blatman estimates the number to be about 500,000 (Blatman, "Netanyahu, This Is What Ethnic Cleansing Really Looks Like"). Whatever the exact number, even Israeli "Old Historians" now admit that during the 1948 war, the Israeli armed forces drove out many of the Palestinians, though they emphasized the action as a military "necessity." For example, see Anita Shapira, ''Israel: A History'', 167–68. In July 2019, the Israeli government sought to cover up the extensive documentary evidence in its state archives that revealed detailed evidence about the extent of the Nakba—even the evidence that had already been published by newspapers and Israeli historians. A Haaretz investigation of the attempted cover-up concluded: "Since early last decade, Defense Ministry teams have scoured local archives and removed troves of historic documents to conceal proof of the Nakba, including Israeli eyewitness reports at the time" (Shezaf, "Burying the Nakba: How Israel Systematically Hides Evidence of 1948 Expulsion of Arabs")."</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=15 May 2018 |title=Why Nakba is the Palestinians' most sombre day, in 100 and 300 words |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-44114385 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240122041924/https://www.bbc.com/news/world-middle-east-44114385 |archive-date=22 January 2024 |work=[[BBC News]] |quote=...{{nbsp}}up to 750,000 Palestinians who had lived on that land fled or were expelled from their homes.}}</ref> during the [[1948 Palestine war]].<ref>{{cite book |last1=McDowall |first1=David |title=The Palestinians |last2=Palley |first2=Claire |publisher=[[Minority Rights Group]] Report no 24 |year=1987 |isbn=978-0-946690-42-8 |page=10}}</ref>

Since the beginning of the Gaza war, nearly 2 million people have been displaced within the Gaza Strip.<ref name="Gdn1912232">{{cite news |last1=Graham-Harrison |first1=Emma |last2=Borger |first2=Julian |date=19 December 2023 |title=Palestinian death toll in Gaza nears 20,000 with nearly 2 million people displaced |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/19/palestinian-casualties-in-gaza-near-20000-with-nearly-2m-people-displaced |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231224201330/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/dec/19/palestinian-casualties-in-gaza-near-20000-with-nearly-2m-people-displaced |archive-date=24 December 2023 |access-date=25 December 2023 |work=[[The Guardian]]}}</ref>{{sfn|El-Affendi|2024|p=6}}

== Alleged international complicity since 2023 ==
{{Main|Gaza genocide#Responsibility of third states and other entities}}

{{See also|Complicity in genocide|United States support for Israel in the Gaza war}}
[[File:Rep Beatty Ohio says Ceasefire now in Columbus, 2023-12-22 (8000-95).jpg|thumb|A protestor in [[Columbus, Ohio]], carrying a sign referring to United States President [[Joe Biden]] as "Genocide Joe", 22 December 2023]]

{{excerpt|Gaza genocide#Responsibility of third states and other entities|only=paragraph}}

[[U.S. National Security Council]] spokesman [[John Kirby (admiral)|John Kirby]], described by Israeli media outlet ''[[Ynet]]'' as "an exceptionally accomplished Israeli advocate",<ref>{{cite news |last1=Shmilovitz |first1=Tzippy |date=18 December 2023 |title=How John Kirby became one of Israel's leading spokespeople |url=https://www.ynetnews.com/magazine/article/rjwja2hlt |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231221195325/https://www.ynetnews.com/magazine/article/rjwja2hlt |archive-date=21 December 2023 |access-date=21 December 2023 |website=[[Ynet News]]}}</ref> said "Israel's trying to defend itself against a genocidal terrorist threat. So if we're going to start using that word, fine, let's use it appropriately".<ref name="Forbes2">{{cite web |date=20 November 2023 |title=White House Asked Point Blank About Pro-Ceasefire Protesters Calling Biden 'Genocide Joe' |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RpiceCp2Cp0 |access-date=20 November 2023 |via=[[YouTube]] |newspaper=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> On 13 November 2023, the New York-based [[Center for Constitutional Rights]] sued Biden for allegedly failing in his duties, defined under national and international laws, to prevent Israel committing genocide in Gaza in the Gaza war.<ref name="McGreal 20232" /> The complaint alleged that Israel's "mass killings", targeting of civilian infrastructure and forced expulsions amounted to genocide.<ref name="McGreal 20232" /><ref name="TIMEBiden2">{{cite magazine |last=Mansoor |first=Sanya |date=21 November 2023 |title=Pro-Palestinian Americans Are Pushing Biden to Pivot |url=https://time.com/6337911/biden-israel-policy-palestine-pressure/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240102191717/https://time.com/6337911/biden-israel-policy-palestine-pressure/ |archive-date=2 January 2024 |access-date=23 November 2023 |magazine=[[Time (magazine)|TIME]] |language=en}}</ref> In a declaration in the lawsuit, genocide scholar [[William Schabas]] said that in his view there was a "serious risk of genocide" and that the US was "in breach of its obligation" under the [[Genocide Convention|1948 Genocide Convention]] and international law.<ref name="TIMEBiden2" /><ref name="CNSBiden2">{{cite web |last=Hanson |first=Natalie |date=23 November 2023 |title=Palestinians file lawsuit accusing Biden administration of violating Genocide Convention |url=https://www.courthousenews.com/palestinians-file-lawsuit-accusing-biden-administration-of-violating-genocide-convention/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231213203151/https://www.courthousenews.com/palestinians-file-lawsuit-accusing-biden-administration-of-violating-genocide-convention/ |archive-date=13 December 2023 |website=[[Courthouse News Service]]}}</ref> In January 2024 a [[United States federal judge|federal judge]] dismissed the case [[Defense for Children International – Palestine et al v. Biden et al]], saying [[Constitution of the United States|the Constitution]] prevents his court from determining foreign policy, which is reserved to the political branches of U.S. government, though he would have preferred to have issued the injunction and urged President Biden to rethink U.S. policy, writing "it is plausible that Israel's conduct amounts to genocide."<ref>{{cite news |last=Hubler |first=Shawn |date=31 January 2024 |title=A federal judge dismisses a suit to block U.S. support of Israel — but urges Biden to re-examine his approach |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/31/world/middleeast/joe-biden-israel-support.html |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240201153444/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/01/31/world/middleeast/joe-biden-israel-support.html%20 |archive-date=1 February 2024 |access-date=1 February 2024 |work=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref> In February 2024, the Lemkin Institute for Genocide Prevention stated the Biden Administration was complicit in the alleged [[Gaza genocide]].<ref>{{cite news |title=In Gaza, Biden administration complicit: Lemkin Institute for Genocide Prevention |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/14/israels-war-on-gaza-live-afraid-to-leave-as-israel-fires-on-hospital?update=2708406 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240214182846/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/14/israels-war-on-gaza-live-afraid-to-leave-as-israel-fires-on-hospital?update=2708406 |archive-date=14 February 2024 |access-date=16 February 2024 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]] |quote=None of the Biden Administration's tactics to deny genocide and avoid accountability will withstand the test of time. President Biden and key administration officials are on a path to be remembered as the principal enablers of one of the worst genocides in the 21st century}}</ref> [[Ali Harb]] wrote that the US has continued to arm and fund the Israeli military while it conducts a genocide.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Harb |first1=Ali |title=Biden is said to be angry at Netanyahu, but US rewards keep coming |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/18/israels-war-on-gaza-live-palestinians-fleeing-rafah-face-israeli-strikes?update=2716692 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240219045326/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/18/israels-war-on-gaza-live-palestinians-fleeing-rafah-face-israeli-strikes?update=2716692 |archive-date=19 February 2024 |access-date=19 February 2024 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]}}</ref> In February 2024, following a U.S. veto of a UN ceasefire resolution, Cuban president [[Miguel Diaz-Canel Bermudez]] stated, "They are accomplices of this genocide of Israel against Palestine".<ref>{{cite news |title=Cuba: US 'accomplices' in devastation of Gaza |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/20/israels-war-on-gaza-live-un-fears-explosion-in-child-deaths-in-gaza?update=2721122 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240221081559/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2024/2/20/israels-war-on-gaza-live-un-fears-explosion-in-child-deaths-in-gaza?update=2721122 |archive-date=21 February 2024 |access-date=21 February 2024 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]}}</ref> 

In February 2024 lawyers representing Palestinians in Germany filed a criminal complaint against various senior politicians including [[Olaf Scholz]], [[Annalena Baerbock]], [[Robert Habeck]], and [[Christian Lindner]] for "aiding and abetting" the genocide in Gaza.<ref>{{cite news |last=Schaer |first=Cathrin |date=23 February 2024 |title=German lawyers sue Scholz, alleging complicity in Gaza 'genocide' |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/23/german-lawyers-sue-politicians-including-scholz-over-complicity-in-gaza |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240224051949/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/23/german-lawyers-sue-politicians-including-scholz-over-complicity-in-gaza |archive-date=24 February 2024 |work=[[Al Jazeera English|Al Jazeera]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |date=23 February 2024 |title=Gaza victims sue German government for 'aiding genocide against Palestinians' |url=https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20240223-gaza-victims-sue-german-government-for-aiding-genocide-against-palestinians/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240224115453/https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20240223-gaza-victims-sue-german-government-for-aiding-genocide-against-palestinians/ |archive-date=24 February 2024 |work=[[Middle East Monitor]]}}</ref> On 1 March 2024, [[Nicaragua v. Germany|Nicaragua instituted proceedings against Germany]] at the ICJ under the Genocide Convention, concerning Germany's support for Israel in the Gaza war.<ref name="mee-2024-1-12"/><ref name="reuters-2024-1-12"/>

In March 2024, Australian Prime Minister [[Anthony Albanese]], Foreign Minister [[Penny Wong]], Opposition Leader [[Peter Dutton]], and others were referred to the ICC by Sydney-based firm Birchgrove Legal as accessories to genocide, war crimes, and crimes against humanity, citing the defunding of [[UNRWA]], the provision of military aid, and "unequivocal political support" for Israel's actions during the Gaza war.<ref>{{cite news |date=5 March 2024 |title=Anthony Albanese dismisses ICC war crimes allegations: Experts weigh in on the claims |url=https://www.sbs.com.au/news/article/anthony-albanese-dismisses-icc-war-crimes-allegations-experts-weigh-in-on-the-claims/xu4kueiql |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240305094219/https://www.sbs.com.au/news/article/anthony-albanese-dismisses-icc-war-crimes-allegations-experts-weigh-in-on-the-claims/xu4kueiql |archive-date=5 March 2024 |access-date=5 March 2024 |work=[[SBS News]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Rothwell |first=Donald |date=5 March 2024 |title=Why have Anthony Albanese and other politicians been referred to the ICC over the Gaza war? |url=http://theconversation.com/why-have-anthony-albanese-and-other-politicians-been-referred-to-the-icc-over-the-gaza-war-225079 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240305092042/https://theconversation.com/why-have-anthony-albanese-and-other-politicians-been-referred-to-the-icc-over-the-gaza-war-225079 |archive-date=5 March 2024 |access-date=5 March 2024 |website=[[The Conversation (website)|The Conversation]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

